ow patterns dominate.', '{"Adventure_travellers","Photographers","Road_trippers"}', '{"Adventure_travellers": "Remote valley and high passes.", "Photographers": "Unique desert and mountain scenery."}'::jsonb, 'Altitude acclimatisation in Leh necessary first; permits needed; limited healthcare locally.', 2.0, 2.0, 3, 'Day 1: Drive from Leh to Nubra via Khardung La; evening dunes and camels; Day 2: Diskit Monastery, village visits and return or continue to Turtuk.', 'Camps | Guesthouses | Homestays | Some higher-end tented camps', 'Simple local and Indian meals; many stays include meals.', 8.0, 'Low crime; high environmental risk; weather and altitude can be harsh.', 'Limited and often slow.', 'Jio in some pockets; otherwise restricted', 'None/very few; withdraw in Leh.', 'Ladakhi | Hindi | Basic English with tourism operators', TRUE, 'Inner Line Permits for Indian citizens and specific protocols for foreigners; check latest guidelines.', 'Mix of Buddhist and Balti influences.', 'Local monastery festivals and village events.', 'Respect local norms and modest dress, especially in villages and monasteries.', 'Small handicrafts | Local dried apricots and produce', 'Momos | Thukpa | Simple local breads and stews', '{"accommodation_range": [700, 1400], "food_range": [300, 600], "activities_range": [300, 700], "local_transport_range": [300, 600], "total_daily_range": [1600, 3300]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1400, 3000], "food_range": [500, 900], "activities_range": [700, 1400], "local_transport_range": [500, 900], "total_daily_range": [3100, 6200]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [5000, 12000], "food_range": [800, 2000], "activities_range": [1200, 2500], "local_transport_range": [700, 1200], "total_daily_range": [7700, 17700]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Nubra Valley in Ladakh.', 'Highlight of many Ladakh trips due to its unusual desert landscape and villages.', 'Growth in luxury camps and improved roads from Leh side.', 'Camel welfare, waste management and water use are key concerns; choose responsible operators.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-18', 'Pangong Lake (Pangong Tso)', 'IN-LA', 'leh', 'Leh', 'North India', 33.79, 78.59, 4350, 8.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Leh Kushok Bakula Rimpochee Airport", "distance_km": 150}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Jammu Tawi", "distance_km": 570}'::jsonb, 'Leh', 150.0, 'Road from Leh via Chang La pass; high altitude and weather-dependent.', '{"Nature","Photography","High_altitude","Camping"}', '{"Colour-changing blue lake","High-altitude landscapes","Nearby village stays (Spangmik area)"}', '{"Lakeside walks","Photography","Simple camping or tent stays","Short hikes around villages"}', 'Stunning colour-shifting lake at over 4000 m with stark mountains all around.', 'Less-crowded stretches of lake accessed by short walks | Small homestays back from main tent rows', 'Summer | Early Autumn', 'Winter and bad weather periods; extremely cold and often inaccessible', 'June–September', 'October–May', '{"winter": "-25--5\u00b0C", "summer": "5-18\u00b0C", "monsoon": "5-16\u00b0C (little rain)"}'::jsonb, 'Very low rainfall; wind and cold are bigger issues.', '{"Landscape_photographers","Adventure_travellers","Short_high_altitude_getaways_from_Leh"}', '{"Landscape_photographers": "Iconic blue lake and barren mountains.", "Adventure_travellers": "High-altitude experience with remote feel."}'::jsonb, 'Altitude risk is real; avoid running or exertion on arrival; very cold nights even in summer; permits required.', 2.0, 2.0, 3, 'Day 1: Drive from Leh over Chang La, reach lake by afternoon; Day 2: Morning by the lake and return to Leh.', 'Tented camps (seasonal) | Homestays in nearby villages | Basic guesthouses', 'Simple meals provided by camps/homestays; limited menu and mostly Indian/Tibetan staples.', 8.0, 'Altitude, cold and remoteness are main risks; border sensitivity in some stretches.', 'Very limited to none for most visitors.', 'Intermittent/none; do not depend on connectivity', 'None; carry cash from Leh.', 'Ladakhi | Hindi | Basic English for tourists', TRUE, 'Inner Line Permit for Indian nationals; specific rules for foreigners; check current regulations in Leh.', 'Sparse settlements with Tibetan Buddhist culture.', 'No major lake-side festivals; region influenced by broader Ladakhi events.', 'Respect environmental norms; avoid entering water in unsafe spots.', 'Very limited; better to shop in Leh | Small local handicrafts in villages', 'Simple thukpa | Momos | Tea and basic homely meals', '{"accommodation_range": [500, 1200], "food_range": [300, 600], "activities_range": [200, 400], "local_transport_range": [3000, 5000], "total_daily_range": [4000, 7200]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1200, 2500], "food_range": [600, 1200], "activities_range": [400, 800], "local_transport_range": [4000, 6000], "total_daily_range": [6200, 10500]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3000, 7000], "food_range": [1200, 2000], "activities_range": [800, 1500], "local_transport_range": [5000, 8000], "total_daily_range": [10000, 18500]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Pangong Lake (Pangong Tso) in Ladakh.', 'Considered one of the most beautiful lakes in India; cold and altitude can be tough but views are exceptional.', 'Better-regulated tented camps, some shifts towards permanent homestays instead of large camps.', 'Waste and over-tourism are concerns; choose low-impact stays and minimise single-use plastic.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
