4\u00b0C", "summer": "26-44\u00b0C", "monsoon": "22-30\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Central Indian monsoon, park shut during heavy-rain period.[web:230]', '{"Serious_wildlife_photographers","Repeat_safari_travellers","Nature_lovers"}', '{"Serious_wildlife_photographers": "High encounter rates with tigers across zones.[web:230]", "Repeat_safari_travellers": "Complements Kanha, Pench and other MP parks in circuit.[web:233]"}'::jsonb, 'High demand for prime zones in season; book safaris well in advance and be prepared for early morning wake-ups in cooler weather.', 2.0, 3.0, 5, 'At least 3–4 safaris split across zones like Tala/Magadhi plus buffer excursions for variety.[web:230][web:233]', 'Jungle resorts | Safari lodges | Homestays in nearby villages', 'Lodge-based dining with Indian and some continental dishes.', 9.0, 'Follow ranger and guide instructions; wildlife is wild and should never be provoked.', 'Resort Wi‑Fi and limited mobile data depending on location.', 'Jio, Airtel (patchy)', 'ATMs in Umaria/nearby towns; carry cash to park area.', 'Hindi | Local dialects | English (guides)', TRUE, 'Safari booking per zone/vehicle with limited seats; ID proof required.[web:230]', 'Rural MP villages with strong connection to forest landscape.', 'Local festivals; some lodges host nature and photography workshops.', 'Respect village life; do not pressure guides to break rules for closer sightings.', 'Wildlife souvenirs | Local crafts via community shops', 'Simple village-style MP thalis', '{"accommodation_range": [1500, 3000], "food_range": [400, 800], "activities_range": [1500, 2500], "local_transport_range": [500, 1000], "total_daily_range": [3900, 7300]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3000, 6000], "food_range": [800, 1500], "activities_range": [2500, 4000], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [7100, 13000]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [6000, 18000], "food_range": [1200, 2500], "activities_range": [3500, 6000], "local_transport_range": [1200, 2000], "total_daily_range": [11900, 28500]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Bandhavgarh National Park in Madhya Pradesh.', 'Known for intense tiger encounters, with many praising guide skills and photographic opportunities.', 'New tourism zones and greater focus on visitor management to reduce pressure on Tala.[web:230]', 'Opt for fewer but longer trips rather than many short safaris; support lodges employing local staff.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
