pril weekends and holidays', 'Late summer heat and monsoon closure', '{"winter": "8-26\u00b0C", "summer": "26-45\u00b0C", "monsoon": "22-30\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Hot, dry summers; distinct monsoon closure period.[web:230]', '{"Quick_safari_from_Nagpur","Wildlife_photographers","Families_who_enjoy_wildlife"}', '{"Quick_safari_from_Nagpur": "Just 2 hours from airport, suitable for shorter wildlife trips.[web:230]", "Wildlife_photographers": "High sighting odds in core zones and diverse species."}'::jsonb, 'Heat can be intense in April–May; choose early-morning safaris and adequate hydration.', 2.0, 3.0, 4, '2–4 safaris over 2–3 days from a base near Moharli or other gates; combine with Nagpur city or other nearby parks if desired.[web:230]', 'Jungle lodges | Resorts | Simple homestays near gates', 'In-resort dining with Maharashtrian and North Indian food.', 9.0, 'Standard tiger-park rules; do not get down from vehicles or approach wildlife.', 'Limited mobile data; some lodges have Wi‑Fi.', 'Jio, Airtel (varies)', 'ATMs in Chandrapur; carry cash to lodge.', 'Marathi | Hindi | English (tourism)', TRUE, 'Advance safari permits with zone allocations; adherence to capacity limits.[web:230]', 'Vidarbha rural communities; some areas with strong forest dependence.', 'Local village festivals; park focuses on safari season cycle.', 'Be respectful when visiting villages; avoid flashy photography of people without consent.', 'Basic souvenirs from lodges | Local snacks and sweets en route', 'Spicy Maharashtrian sabzis and bhakri', '{"accommodation_range": [1500, 3000], "food_range": [400, 800], "activities_range": [1500, 2500], "local_transport_range": [500, 1000], "total_daily_range": [3900, 7300]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3000, 6000], "food_range": [800, 1500], "activities_range": [2500, 4000], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [7100, 13000]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [6000, 18000], "food_range": [1200, 2500], "activities_range": [3500, 6000], "local_transport_range": [1200, 2000], "total_daily_range": [11900, 28500]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Tadoba Andhari Tiger Reserve in Maharashtra.', 'Regularly mentioned for reliable tiger sightings and convenient access from Nagpur.', 'Improved core–buffer management and diversification of entry gates.[web:230]', 'Stick to eco-sensitive lodges, support community guides and minimise plastic use.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-49', 'Lakshadweep (Agatti–Bangaram–Kadmat circuit)', 'IN-LA', 'union-territory-islands', 'Union Territory Islands', 'Island Territory', 10.83, 72.19, 0, 7.0, 'Difficult', '{"name": "Agatti Airport", "distance_km": 0}'::jsonb, '{"name": "None (island chain; access via flights/ships from Kochi)", "distance_km": null}'::jsonb, 'Kochi (main mainland gateway)', 460.0, 'Internal island roads and walking paths only; inter-island travel by boats and ships arranged through administration/tour operators.[web:231][web:234]', '{"Island","Beach","Diving","Honeymoon","Offbeat"}', '{"Agatti Island beaches and lagoon","Bangaram Island (often via permits/packages)","Kadmat Island for water sports and reefs","Kalpeni/Kavaratti side trips depending on itinerary"}', '{"Snorkelling, scuba diving and kayaking in lagoons","Lagoon boat rides and reef walks","Beach relaxation and low-key cycling/walks"}', 'Tropical atolls with turquoise lagoons and vibrant coral reefs that remain far less crowded than other Indian beach destinations.[web:231][web:234]', 'Uninhabited islets near Kalpeni such as Tilakkam, Pitti and Cheriyam (visited via authorised trips).[web:234] | Quiet sunrise/sunset spots on narrow sand spits of Kadmat/Bangaram', 'Dry, calm-sea months from October–March; some itineraries also run through April.[web:231][web:234]', 'Southwest monsoon (rough seas, limited access) and cyclone-alert periods.[web:231]', 'December–March and New Year weeks', 'Monsoon months and shoulder periods with choppy seas', '{"winter": "24-30\u00b0C", "summer": "26-33\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-30\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Heavy monsoon with strong winds; most tourism structured outside wettest months.[web:231]', '{"Honeymooners","Divers_and_snorkellers","Quiet_beach_seekers"}', '{"Honeymooners": "Pristine, uncrowded islands and limited outside distractions.[web:231]", "Divers_and_snorkellers": "Healthy coral reefs and clear lagoons around islands like Kadmat and Bangaram.[web:231][web:234]"}'::jsonb, 'Entry permits and package bookings via authorised operators are mandatory; alcohol availability extremely restricted; cultural sensitivity important.', 4.0, 5.0, 7, 'Fly Kochi–Agatti, spend 1–2 nights, then boat to Bangaram/Kadmat for diving and lagoon time, returning to Agatti for departure based on current package structures.[web:231][web:234]', 'Government-approved resorts | Designated tourist huts | Package-based stays on specific islands', 'Resort and camp kitchens serving South Indian, seafood and simple continental dishes.[web:231]', 9.0, 'Islands are safe; biggest risks are sea/weather conditions—follow authority advisories strictly.', 'Limited; some resorts offer basic connectivity but expect digital detox.[web:231]', 'BSNL primary; some roaming on others where available', 'Very limited; carry adequate cash as per operator guidance.', 'Malayalam | English (administration/tourism) | Hindi (some)', TRUE, 'Entry permits issued via Lakshadweep administration and tour operators; foreigners face additional restrictions.[web:231][web:234]', 'Predominantly Muslim island communities with conservative norms; tourism is tightly regulated.', 'Local Islamic festivals; tourism structured more by season than by events.', 'Dress modestly away from resort beaches; respect no-alcohol norms and local prayer times.', 'Coir products | Shell crafts (ensure they are legally sourced) | Packaged coconut and fish products', 'Fresh fish fries and curries | Coconut-rich island dishes | Traditional Malabari-influenced snacks', '{"accommodation_range": [2500, 5000], "food_range": [600, 1200], "activities_range": [1000, 2500], "local_transport_range": [800, 2000], "total_daily_range": [4900, 10700]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [5000, 9000], "food_range": [1000, 2000], "activities_range": [2000, 4000], "local_transport_range": [1200, 3000], "total_daily_range": [9200, 18000]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [9000, 20000], "food_range": [1500, 3000], "activities_range": [3000, 6000], "local_transport_range": [2000, 4000], "total_daily_range": [15500, 33000]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Lakshadweep (Agatti–Bangaram–Kadmat circuit) in Lakshadweep.', 'Often described as stunning and serene, with special praise for water clarity and reefs but acknowledgment of higher costs and permit complexity.', 'Increased interest within India in 2025; authorities emphasise controlled, eco-sensitive tourism.[web:231][web:234]', 'Coral islands are extremely fragile—use reef-safe sunscreen, never touch corals, and follow strict no-litter rules.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-50', 'Kalpeni Island (Lakshadweep)', 'IN-LA', 'union-territory-islands', 'Union Territory Islands', 'Island Territory', 10.07, 73.65, 0, 5.0, 'Difficult', '{"name": "Agatti Airport (via ship/boat connection)", "distance_km": 150}'::jsonb, '{"name": "None; access via Kochi then ship/boat", "distance_km": null}'::jsonb, 'Kochi (mainland gateway)', 380.0, 'Small internal roads within island; access via ships and boats as part of Lakshadweep itineraries.[web:231][web:234]', '{"Island","Water_sports","Offbeat","Beach"}', '{"Wide shallow lagoon with clear waters","Unique shoreline shaped by coral debris","Nearby uninhabited islets like Tilakkam, Pitti, Cheriyam accessible by authorised trips"}', '{"Kayaking, sailing and reef walks","Snorkelling and basic diving experiences (where offered)","Beach walks and sunrise/sunset watching"}', 'Lagoon-focused island dubbed a ‘lagoon of wonders’ with shallow, wide lagoons ideal for non-swimmers and gentle water activities.[web:231][web:234]', 'Boat trips to close-by tiny islets with pristine sandbars.[web:234] | Quiet night skies with minimal light pollution', 'October–March when seas are calmer and lagoons easily accessible.[web:231][web:234]', 'Monsoon and stormy periods when boat connectivity and activities are restricted.[web:231]', 'December–February', 'Monsoon months and rough-sea spells', '{"winter": "24-30\u00b0C", "summer": "26-33\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-30\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Heavy rains in monsoon; tourism structured around dry months.[web:231]', '{"Families_with_kids","Soft_adventure","Offbeat_island_lovers"}', '{"Families_with_kids": "Shallow lagoons and gentle water-based activities suited to beginners.[web:234]", "Offbeat_island_lovers": "Less-visited than flagship islands like Bangaram/Kadmat."}'::jsonb, 'Part of tightly controlled Lakshadweep tourism; must travel with approved packages; respect conservative local culture.', 2.0, 2.0, 4, 'Typically included as 1–3 night segment in multi-island Lakshadweep package with focus on reef walks, kayaking and islet excursions.[web:231][web:234]', 'Government/tour-operator managed tourist huts | Limited resort-style stays where available', 'Set meals within packages, featuring South Indian staples and fresh seafood.[web:231]', 9.0, 'Very calm if local safety rules followed; heed lifeguards and avoid venturing out independently in rough weather.', 'Minimal; expect near-complete digital detox.[web:234]', 'Primarily BSNL, weak and unreliable', 'None on island; payments usually arranged through package operators.', 'Malayalam | English (administration/tourism)', TRUE, 'Same Lakshadweep entry permit regime; movement handled via official tours.[web:231][web:234]', 'Small Muslim island community with traditional lifestyle.', 'Local religious observances; tourism is quiet and nature-focused.', 'Dress modestly away from tourist-beach areas; follow island administration guidelines.', 'Very limited; small local shops for essentials only', 'Island fish curries with coconut | Local snacks served at tourist huts', '{"accommodation_range": [2000, 4000], "food_range": [500, 1000], "activities_range": [800, 2000], "local_transport_range": [600, 1600], "total_daily_range": [3900, 8600]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4000, 7000], "food_range": [800, 1500], "activities_range": [1500, 3000], "local_transport_range": [800, 2000], "total_daily_range": [7100, 13500]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [7000, 15000], "food_range": [1200, 2500], "activities_range": [2500, 5000], "local_transport_range": [1500, 3000], "total_daily_range": [12200, 25500]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Kalpeni Island (Lakshadweep) in Lakshadweep.', 'Appreciated for peaceful lagoons and uncrowded feel; often called a hidden gem within an already offbeat archipelago.', 'More structured inclusion in Lakshadweep tour circuits with emphasis on low-impact activities.[web:234]', 'Reefs and islets are extremely fragile—strictly avoid litter, coral contact and unsupervised exploration.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-51', 'Jaisalmer (Thar Desert & Fort Town)', 'IN-RJ', 'jaisalmer', 'Jaisalmer', 'North India', 26.9157, 70.9083, 225, 9.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Jaisalmer Airport (seasonal flights) / Jodhpur Airport", "distance_km": 15}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Jaisalmer Junction", "distance_km": 2}'::jsonb, 'Jodhpur', 280.0, 'Good highways from Jodhpur and Bikaner; buses and cabs available, desert stretches beyond town by road/jeep.[web:238][web:241]', '{"Desert","Heritage","Photography","Festival"}', '{"Jaisalmer Fort (living fort with havelis and temples)","Patwon Ki Haveli and other mansions","Sam and Khuri sand dunes (camel and jeep safaris)","Gadisar Lake"}', '{"Fort and haveli walks","Camel/jeep safaris with dune sunset","Overnight desert camping","Shopping for textiles and handicrafts"}', 'Golden sandstone fort city rising from Thar Desert with dune safaris and stargazing at desert camps.[web:238][web:241]', 'Less-touristy Khuri dunes vs busier Sam | Quiet inner lanes and rooftop viewpoints in the fort', 'Winter and post-monsoon (October–March).', 'Peak summer for extreme heat; occasional dust storms; check festival crowd levels if seeking quiet.[web:238]', 'November–February and during Jaisalmer Desert Festival dates in February.[web:235][web:237][web:241]', 'April–September (very hot; some camps shut in off months)', '{"winter": "7-26\u00b0C", "summer": "28-45\u00b0C", "monsoon": "26-34\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Very low rainfall desert climate; rare but intense showers possible in monsoon.[web:238]', '{"Couples","Friends_groups","Photography_enthusiasts","Culture_lovers"}', '{"Photography_enthusiasts": "Golden fort, blue skies, dunes and desert night skies.", "Culture_lovers": "Folk music, dance and desert festival events with camel races and competitions.[web:235][web:238][web:241]"}'::jsonb, 'Desert nights can get cold in winter; advanced booking needed for festival period; choose ethical camel operators.', 2.0, 3.0, 4, 'Day 1: Fort, havelis and lake; Day 2: Sam/Khuri dunes with sunset and camping; Day 3: Extra fort areas, desert village trip or festival events if in February.[web:235][web:237][web:238][web:241]', 'Fort-view hotels | Budget guesthouses | Desert camps (basic to luxury) | Heritage havelis', 'Rajasthani thalis, local snacks and rooftop restaurants with fort views.', 8.0, 'Town and camps are generally safe; protect from sun and dehydration in desert.', 'Good 4G in town; weaker at remote dune camps.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in Jaisalmer town; none at dunes.', 'Hindi | Rajasthani | English (tourism)', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Desert trading and warrior heritage with strong folk-art traditions.', 'Jaisalmer Desert Festival in February with camel races, folk performances, turban tying, moustache and Mr Desert contests.[web:235][web:237][web:238][web:241]', 'Dress modestly in old town; remove shoes at temples; tip folk performers fairly.', 'Mirror-work textiles | Camel-leather items | Rajasthani jewellery and puppets', 'Dal baati churma | Ker sangri | Gatte ki sabzi', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 1500], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [400, 1000], "local_transport_range": [200, 500], "total_daily_range": [1650, 3500]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1500, 3500], "food_range": [400, 800], "activities_range": [800, 1500], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [3000, 6500]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3500, 15000], "food_range": [800, 2000], "activities_range": [1500, 3000], "local_transport_range": [500, 1200], "total_daily_range": [6300, 21200]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Jaisalmer (Thar Desert & Fort Town) in Rajasthan.', 'Often described as a highlight of Rajasthan for its fairy-tale fort and desert experiences; some find festival crowds intense but enjoyable.', 'Better structured festival programmes and more organised desert camps near Sam and Khuri.[web:235][web:238][web:241]', 'Desert ecosystem is fragile; avoid littering dunes and support camps that manage waste and limit water use.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-52', 'Kutch Interior Circuit (Bhuj–Mandvi–Villages)', 'IN-GJ', 'kachchh', 'Kachchh', 'West India', 23.25, 69.67, 60, 6.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Bhuj Airport", "distance_km": 5}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Bhuj", "distance_km": 5}'::jsonb, 'Bhuj', 0.0, 'Good roads from Bhuj to Mandvi, Kala Dungar and craft villages like Hodka, Nirona and Bhujodi.[web:210]', '{"Cultural","Desert_coastal","Handicrafts","Road_trip"}', '{"Bhuj old town and palaces","Mandvi beach and Vijay Vilas Palace","Craft villages (Bhujodi, Nirona, Hodka, etc.)","Kala Dungar hill and nearby desert landscapes"}', '{"Handicraft village visits and shopping","Beach walks at Mandvi","Short hikes/drives to viewpoints","Local food exploration"}', 'Mix of palaces, coastal beaches and famous artisan villages producing textiles, Rogan art and embroidery, complementing White Rann visits.[web:210]', 'Lesser-known craft villages where you can watch artisans at work | Quiet stretches of Mandvi beach beyond main crowd', 'Winter and Rann Utsav period (October–March).', 'Peak summer afternoons and humid monsoon days; some craft activity slows in extreme weather.[web:210]', 'Rann Utsav months and long weekends', 'Hot off-peak months and monsoon', '{"winter": "12-28\u00b0C", "summer": "28-42\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Semi-arid with light to moderate monsoon rainfall.', '{"Handicraft_shoppers","Culture_lovers","Road_trippers"}', '{"Handicraft_shoppers": "Direct-from-artisan buying in weaving, Rogan art and embroidery villages.[web:210]", "Road_trippers": "Easy loops Bhuj\u2013Mandvi\u2013villages\u2013Kala Dungar with desert and coastal scenery."}'::jsonb, 'Homestays and village stays may have simpler amenities; modest dress appreciated in rural areas.', 3.0, 4.0, 6, 'Day 1: Bhuj town sights; Day 2: Mandvi beach and palace; Day 3–4: Craft villages and Kala Dungar; optionally combine with White Rann stay in Dhordo.[web:210]', 'City hotels in Bhuj | Village homestays | Heritage and beach resorts near Mandvi', 'Gujarati thalis, snacks and local coastal dishes; simple village meals in homestays.', 8.0, 'Generally safe rural region; heat exposure main concern in summer.', 'Good in Bhuj and Mandvi; weaker in remote villages.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in Bhuj and Mandvi; carry cash to villages.', 'Gujarati | Hindi | English (some)', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Strong craft traditions and Kutchi cultural identity with Hindu and Muslim artisan communities.', 'Overlap with Rann Utsav and local fairs; Navratri and other Gujarati festivals widely celebrated.[web:210]', 'Ask before photographing artisans; buy directly where possible to support livelihoods.', 'Kutchi embroidery and textiles | Rogan art paintings | Bandhani, shawls and stoles', 'Gujarati thali | Kutchi Dabeli | Local sweets like mawa-based desserts', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 1800], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [300, 700], "local_transport_range": [400, 800], "total_daily_range": [1750, 3800]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1800, 3500], "food_range": [400, 800], "activities_range": [700, 1400], "local_transport_range": [600, 1200], "total_daily_range": [3500, 6900]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3500, 9000], "food_range": [700, 1600], "activities_range": [1400, 2500], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [6400, 14600]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Kutch Interior Circuit (Bhuj–Mandvi–Villages) in Gujarat.', 'Appreciated as a rich cultural extension to White Rann trips, especially for handicraft and heritage lovers.', 'Better road signage and more curated craft tours from Bhuj.[web:210]', 'Respect artisans’ time and avoid heavy bargaining for handwork; carry your own bottle and minimise plastic in villages.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
