for full waterfalls and mist; shoulder months for calmer weather.[web:243]', 'Extremely heavy-rain alert days with landslide or road-closure risk; respect all IMD alerts.[web:243]', 'July–August weekends', 'Dry winter and summer with fewer waterfalls', '{"winter": "14-26\u00b0C", "summer": "20-32\u00b0C", "monsoon": "18-24\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'One of Maharashtra’s wettest ghats with persistent rain and fog in peak season.[web:243]', '{"Monsoon_chasers","Macro_and_herp_photographers","Short_break_travellers_from_Belagavi/Goa"}', '{"Monsoon_chasers": "Waterfalls right by the road and dense, mossy forests.", "Macro_and_herp_photographers": "Diverse small fauna in rainforest conditions (with guides)."}'::jsonb, 'High leech, slippery rocks and low visibility; only skilled drivers should attempt ghat in very heavy rain.', 1.0, 2.0, 3, 'Overnight or weekend trip: day drives along ghat, waterfall stops and night macro walks with experts.', 'Basic hotels | Small resorts | Homestays', 'Simple Maharashtrian and Konkan dishes in local eateries.', 7.0, 'Slippery roads and cliffs; avoid risky selfies at falls and never enter strong currents.[web:243]', 'Basic mobile data in town; weak in inner forest sections.', 'Jio | Airtel, variable', 'Few ATMs nearby; withdraw in larger towns.', 'Marathi | Konkani | Hindi', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Konkan–Maharashtra hill communities; agriculture and small tourism.', 'Local temple festivals; monsoon weekends effectively become an event for visitors.', 'Respect local advice on safe waterfall access; dress modestly in village areas.', 'Local snacks | Spices from Konkan', 'Kombdi vade and fish fry (for non-vegetarians) | Simple Maharashtrian veg thali', '{"accommodation_range": [700, 1500], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [200, 500], "local_transport_range": [300, 600], "total_daily_range": [1450, 3100]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1500, 3500], "food_range": [400, 800], "activities_range": [400, 800], "local_transport_range": [400, 800], "total_daily_range": [2700, 5900]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3500, 9000], "food_range": [700, 1500], "activities_range": [600, 1500], "local_transport_range": [600, 1200], "total_daily_range": [5400, 16200]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Amboli Ghat in Maharashtra.', 'Beloved by monsoon enthusiasts; some warn about crowding at main falls on weekends and slippery conditions.', 'Increased safety signage and social-media awareness about flood and landslide warnings.[web:243]', 'Do not throw plastic in waterfalls or forests; respect nocturnal wildlife during herping trips.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-59', 'Agumbe & Western Ghats Rainforest Belt', 'IN-KA', 'shivamogga-udupi-region', 'Shivamogga / Udupi region', 'South India', 13.5, 75.08, 650, 5.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Mangaluru Airport", "distance_km": 100}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Udupi / Shivamogga", "distance_km": 55}'::jsonb, 'Mangaluru', 100.0, 'Hairpin Ghat roads from Udupi/Mangaluru side and interior Karnataka; buses and cabs available.[web:240]', '{"Rainforest","Monsoon","Herping_macro","Offbeat"}', '{"Sunset viewpoints over Arabian Sea side","Nearby waterfalls such as Barkana, Onake Abbi (trek-based, regulated)","High-rainfall evergreen forests rich in wildlife"}', '{"Forest treks with guides (permits as required)","Monsoon and post-monsoon herping and macro photography","Village homestay experiences"}', 'One of India’s wettest regions with dense rainforests, king cobra research area and dramatic Ghats sunsets.[web:240]', 'Research-station guided walks where accessible | Less-commercial homestays deep in Ghats', 'Monsoon and immediately after (June–October) for rainforest atmosphere; winter for drier treks.[web:240]', 'Severe weather spells with official landslide/flood alerts; some trails are closed in heavy monsoon.[web:240]', 'Monsoon weekends for enthusiasts; winter for general trekking', 'Hotter pre-monsoon weeks', '{"winter": "14-26\u00b0C", "summer": "22-32\u00b0C", "monsoon": "18-26\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Extremely high rainfall; frequent downpours and low clouds.[web:240]', '{"Nature_research_and_herp_fans","Serious_monson_chasers","Offbeat_travellers"}', '{"Nature_research_and_herp_fans": "King cobra and amphibian diversity studied here; specialised tours available.", "Serious_monson_chasers": "Deep rainforest monsoon feel, not just roadside showers."}'::jsonb, 'Permits and local-guide requirements for many treks; leeches are common; must follow forest department regulations strictly.', 2.0, 3.0, 5, 'Base at homestay; allocate days to one waterfall trek, one rainforest/herping-focused night walk (with experts) and one sunset viewpoint drive.[web:240]', 'Homestays | Eco-lodges | Basic guesthouses', 'Simple home-style Karnataka and coastal-influenced meals at homestays.', 7.0, 'Steep, slippery trails; venomous snakes present—always be with guides and wear suitable footwear.', 'Limited; consider stay as semi-digital-detox.', 'Patchy Jio/Airtel; BSNL in some spots', 'ATMs in larger nearby towns; none in deep interior.', 'Kannada | Tulu (coastal) | English (some) | Hindi (some)', TRUE, 'Forest department permissions for treks and some viewpoints; local homestays often arrange.[web:240]', 'Rural Western Ghats communities with agriculture and forest-linked livelihoods.', 'Local temple festivals; scientific events related to rainforest research occasionally.', 'Follow homestay rules; be quiet at night to respect wildlife and village life.', 'Limited; pick up spices or local produce via homestays', 'Local rice and sambar meals | Coastal-style fish (in non-veg homes)', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 1800], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [300, 700], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [1650, 3700]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1800, 3500], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [700, 1400], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [3300, 6700]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3500, 9000], "food_range": [800, 2000], "activities_range": [1200, 2500], "local_transport_range": [600, 1200], "total_daily_range": [6100, 16700]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Agumbe & Western Ghats Rainforest Belt in Karnataka.', 'Loved by niche travellers who enjoy rainforests and solitude; casual tourists may find heavy rain and basic amenities challenging.', 'Careful promotion as eco-tourism and research hub to avoid over-commercialisation.[web:240]', 'Rainforest is extremely sensitive; stay only with responsible operators, avoid plastic and strictly stay on permitted trails.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-60', 'Kudremukh & Surrounding Ghats', 'IN-KA', 'chikkamagaluru', 'Chikkamagaluru', 'South India', 13.13, 75.25, 1600, 6.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Mangaluru Airport", "distance_km": 100}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Mangalore Junction", "distance_km": 95}'::jsonb, 'Mangaluru', 100.0, 'Ghat roads from Mangaluru, Chikmagalur and Sringeri with forest check-posts and regulated access to national park area.[web:240]', '{"Trekking","Rainforest","Offbeat","Nature"}', '{"Kudremukh peak trek (regulated)","Rolling grassland and shola forest landscapes","Nearby waterfalls and streams"}', '{"Full-day guided treks to Kudremukh peak (with permits)","Shorter hikes and stream visits","Birding and nature walks"}', 'Iconic horse-face shaped mountain amid grassland–forest mosaic, considered one of Karnataka’s most beautiful treks.', 'Smaller peaks and trails in buffer area | Homestays in villages like Mullodi that serve as trek bases', 'Post-monsoon (October–February) for clear views; monsoon for dramatic clouds but restricted trekking windows.[web:240]', 'Days with heavy rain/landslide alerts; core trek often closed or controlled during worst monsoon spells.[web:240]', 'October–January weekends', 'Peak monsoon and hottest pre-monsoon days', '{"winter": "12-22\u00b0C", "summer": "18-30\u00b0C", "monsoon": "16-24\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Very high rainfall during monsoon; lush greenery and strong streams afterwards.[web:240]', '{"Fit_trekkers","Nature_photographers","Small_friend_groups"}', '{"Fit_trekkers": "Kudremukh trail is moderately challenging but hugely rewarding in views.", "Nature_photographers": "Rolling hills, mist and streams create classic Western Ghats frames."}'::jsonb, 'Daily trek quotas and permits managed by forest department; must start early with guide; leeches in monsoon; pack light but with rain and sun protection.', 2.0, 2.0, 4, 'Day 1: Reach homestay base and short acclimatisation walk; Day 2: Kudremukh peak trek; extra day(s) for nearby smaller treks and waterfalls.[web:240]', 'Homestays in villages | Basic eco-stays | Lodges in nearby small towns', 'Simple, hearty home-cooked Karnataka meals at homestays.', 8.0, 'Trek only with authorised guides; weather can change quickly; streams may swell in rain.', 'Limited; some homestays have basic network coverage.', 'Patchy Jio/Airtel; BSNL in some points', 'ATMs in larger towns before entering interior belt.', 'Kannada | Tulu (some) | English (some) | Hindi (some)', TRUE, 'Trek permits and visitor limits per day; issued via forest department/registered homestays.[web:240]', 'Farming and plantation villages in Western Ghats foothills.', 'Local temple festivals; nature is main draw.', 'Respect homestay rules and quiet hours; no alcohol or loud music in forest zones.', 'Limited; perhaps coffee/spices from nearby towns', 'Simple rice–sambar meals | Local vegetable preparations', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 1800], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [300, 700], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [1650, 3700]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1800, 4000], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [700, 1400], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [3300, 7200]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4000, 9000], "food_range": [800, 2000], "activities_range": [1200, 2500], "local_transport_range": [600, 1200], "total_daily_range": [6600, 14700]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Kudremukh & Surrounding Ghats in Karnataka.', 'Kudremukh trek is consistently rated among the best day treks in South India; restrictions are seen as positive for conservation.', 'Stricter trek caps and more emphasis on guide-led, eco-friendly trekking.[web:240]', 'Pack out all waste, stay on official trails and follow forest-department instructions strictly.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-63', 'Port Blair & Nearby Islands', 'IN-AN', 'south-andaman', 'South Andaman', 'Island Territory', 11.67, 92.75, 0, 8.0, 'Easy', '{"name": "Veer Savarkar International Airport, Port Blair", "distance_km": 3}'::jsonb, '{"name": "None", "distance_km": null}'::jsonb, 'Chennai / Kolkata (mainland gateways by air)', 1300.0, 'Town roads with taxis, autos and rented two-wheelers; primary gateway by flights and ships from mainland.[web:244][web:245][web:247]', '{"Gateway_city","History","Island","Family"}', '{"Cellular Jail and sound-and-light show","Corbyn’s Cove Beach","Ross Island (Netaji Subhash Chandra Bose Island) boat trip","Museums and local markets"}', '{"Historical tours","Short island-hopping by boat","Local food and market walks","Intro glass-bottom or snorkelling excursions"}', 'Historic port town that frames Andaman’s freedom-struggle narrative while acting as the logistics hub for island-hopping.[web:244][web:245][web:247]', 'Small cafes and eateries overlooking harbour | Less-known viewpoints on nearby hills', 'October–April aligning with Andaman high season.[web:244][web:245]', 'Rough-sea monsoon spells that affect boat operations and outdoor sightseeing.[web:244]', 'December–March and school holidays.[web:245]', 'Monsoon and lower-traffic shoulder months', '{"winter": "24-30\u00b0C", "summer": "26-33\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-30\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Heavy tropical rains; sightseeing sometimes rearranged around showers.[web:244]', '{"History_buffs","Families","First_time_Andaman_visitors"}', '{"History_buffs": "Cellular Jail and related museums tell the story of political prisoners.[web:244]", "First_time_Andaman_visitors": "Good place to acclimatise, arrange ferries and sample local food.[web:245]"}'::jsonb, 'Sound-and-light show tickets and Ross Island boats may need advance booking in peak season.[web:244]', 1.0, 2.0, 3, 'Half–one day for Cellular Jail, Corbyn’s and markets; one day for Ross Island and nearby spots before heading to Havelock/Neil.[web:245]', 'City hotels (budget to premium) | Guesthouses | Government-run options', 'Mix of South Indian, North Indian and seafood restaurants plus bakeries and cafes.[web:244]', 9.0, 'Safe small city; usual precautions suffice; follow boat safety rules.', 'Best internet in Andamans but still slower than mainland; 4G improving.[web:244]', 'BSNL, Jio, Airtel with expanding coverage.[web:244]', 'Multiple ATMs and banks across town.[web:244]', 'Hindi | Bengali | Tamil | Telugu | English widely used.[web:244]', TRUE, 'Standard entry process at airport; Restricted Area Permit regime is integrated into arrival for most Indian tourists.[web:244]', 'Multi-ethnic island capital with diverse communities and seafaring orientation.[web:244]', 'National days are marked strongly at Cellular Jail; local versions of mainland festivals.', 'Photography may be restricted in some government/defence areas; follow posted signs.[web:244]', 'Shell crafts (avoid illegal coral/shell collection) | Spices and packaged coconut products | Small handicrafts and T‑shirts', 'Seafood thalis | South Indian breakfasts | Local-style fish curries', '{"accommodation_range": [1200, 3000], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [600, 1500], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [2600, 6300]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3000, 7000], "food_range": [800, 1500], "activities_range": [1000, 2500], "local_transport_range": [600, 1500], "total_daily_range": [5400, 12500]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [7000, 18000], "food_range": [1200, 2500], "activities_range": [2000, 4000], "local_transport_range": [1000, 2000], "total_daily_range": [11200, 26500]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Port Blair & Nearby Islands in Andaman and Nicobar Islands.', 'Viewed as a practical and interesting starting/ending point rather than a pure beach destination, with high praise for Cellular Jail experience.[web:245][web:247]', 'Infrastructure upgrades, improved waterfront areas and more organised island tours.[web:244]', 'Support regulated operators, avoid littering sea-fronts and skip buying items made from coral or protected shells.[web:244]') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-64', 'Darjeeling', 'IN-WB', 'darjeeling', 'Darjeeling', 'East India', 27.04, 88.26, 2045, 9.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Bagdogra Airport (Siliguri)", "distance_km": 70}'::jsonb, '{"name": "New Jalpaiguri (NJP)", "distance_km": 75}'::jsonb, 'Siliguri', 65.0, 'Hill roads and shared jeeps from Siliguri/NJP/Bagdogra; iconic Darjeeling Himalayan Railway operates on a narrow-gauge route.[web:248][web:251]', '{"Hill_station","Tea_gardens","Heritage","Family","Honeymoon"}', '{"Tiger Hill sunrise views of Kanchenjunga (weather permitting)","Tea gardens and factory visits","Batasia Loop and Toy Train rides","Mall Road and Observatory Hill area"}', '{"Toy train joyrides","Tea estate tours","Short walks and viewpoints","Monastery visits"}', 'Colonial-era hill station with UNESCO-listed Himalayan Railway and world-famous tea estates facing the Eastern Himalayas.[web:248][web:251][web:249][web:252]', 'Smaller tea gardens that allow slower, less commercial visits | Quiet walks towards nearby villages away from main market', 'March–June and October–November for views and pleasant weather.[web:248][web:251]', 'Peak monsoon for landslide risks and clouded views; some winter weeks can be very cold and foggy.', 'Summer holidays (April–June) and Durga Puja/Diwali periods.[web:248][web:251]', 'Deep monsoon and some mid-winter weeks', '{"winter": "2-12\u00b0C", "summer": "10-22\u00b0C", "monsoon": "10-18\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Heavy monsoon rains affect road conditions and visibility.[web:248]', '{"Families","Couples","Tea_and_heritage_lovers"}', '{"Tea_and_heritage_lovers": "Historic estates and the Darjeeling Himalayan Railway heritage ride.[web:248][web:249][web:252]", "Families": "Easy sightseeing, toy train and viewpoints suit varied ages.[web:251]"}'::jsonb, 'Road closures due to landslides sometimes affect access; always check local advisories in monsoon.', 2.0, 3.0, 5, 'Day 1: Town walk and Mall area; Day 2: Tiger Hill sunrise and Batasia Loop/toy train; Day 3+: Tea estate tours and monastery/nearby village visits.[web:248][web:251]', 'Budget hotels and guesthouses | Heritage hotels | Tea estate bungalows (nearby)', 'North Indian, Tibetan, Nepali and continental cafes and bakeries.', 8.0, 'Generally safe; main issues are steep roads and occasional political/strike-related disruptions.', 'Good 4G in town; weaker in remote tea estates.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in town centre and nearby areas.', 'Nepali | Bengali | Hindi | English (tourism).[web:248][web:251]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Gorkha-majority hill culture with Tibetan and Bengali influences.', 'Local hill festivals and pan-Indian celebrations; tea plucking seasons add interest.', 'Respect monastery rules and avoid loud behaviour in residential hill lanes.', 'Darjeeling tea | Hand-knit woollens | Local handicrafts and souvenirs', 'Momos and thukpa | Darjeeling tea at source | Local Nepali dishes', '{"accommodation_range": [900, 2000], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [300, 800], "local_transport_range": [300, 600], "total_daily_range": [1750, 3900]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2000, 4500], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [700, 1500], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [3500, 7800]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4500, 15000], "food_range": [800, 2000], "activities_range": [1200, 2500], "local_transport_range": [600, 1200], "total_daily_range": [7100, 20700]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Darjeeling in West Bengal.', 'Remains a classic mountain destination with nostalgic charm; some mention congestion in peak months but views and tea culture compensate.[web:248][web:251]', 'More structured tea and heritage packages that combine Darjeeling with Sikkim and nearby areas.[web:248][web:251]', 'Support heritage railway and tea estates with ethical labour practices; avoid plastic on hill trails.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-65', 'Gangtok & East Sikkim', 'IN-SK', 'east-sikkim', 'East Sikkim', 'North East India', 27.33, 88.61, 1650, 8.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Pakyong (limited operations) / Bagdogra", "distance_km": 125}'::jsonb, '{"name": "New Jalpaiguri (NJP)", "distance_km": 120}'::jsonb, 'Siliguri', 115.0, 'Mountain roads from Siliguri/NJP via Teesta valley; shared cabs and private taxis common.[web:248][web:251]', '{"Hill_station","Culture","Monasteries","Family"}', '{"MG Marg promenade","Tsomgo (Changu) Lake and Baba Mandir (permits required)","Tashi View Point and nearby monasteries","Cable car and city viewpoints"}', '{"City walks and cafe-hopping","Day trips to Tsomgo Lake and Nathu La (if open)","Monastery and viewpoint visits"}', 'Clean, organised hill capital acting as a base for wider Sikkim exploration with strong Buddhist influence and valley views.[web:248][web:251][web:249][web:252]', 'Less-touristed monasteries and viewpoints around outskirts | Local bakeries and small eateries off MG Marg', 'March–June and October–December for clear views and comfortable temperatures.[web:248][web:251]', 'Peak monsoon for landslide risk; some high passes close in winter due to snow.', 'Summer vacations and Durga Puja/Diwali corridors.[web:248][web:251]', 'Deep monsoon and some winter weeks', '{"winter": "4-14\u00b0C", "summer": "12-24\u00b0C", "monsoon": "12-20\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'High rainfall in monsoon; frequent cloud and mist on valley roads.[web:248]', '{"Families","First_time_Sikkim_travellers","Monastery_and_culture_lovers"}', '{"First_time_Sikkim_travellers": "Easy logistics and many day-trip options.[web:248][web:251]", "Monastery_and_culture_lovers": "Multiple monasteries and proximity to Khangchendzonga views.[web:249][web:252]"}'::jsonb, 'Permits mandatory for Tsomgo, Nathu La and certain border areas; travel agents usually arrange.[web:248][web:251]', 2.0, 3.0, 5, 'Day 1: MG Marg and local sights; Day 2: Tsomgo Lake/Baba Mandir loop; Day 3+: monasteries and viewpoints or onward travel to North/West Sikkim.[web:248][web:251]', 'Hotels and boutique stays in town | Homestays in nearby villages', 'Combination of Tibetan, Nepali and Indian dishes plus modern cafes.', 9.0, 'City itself is safe; main concerns are road conditions and high-altitude effects on certain day trips.', 'Good 4G coverage in city; weaker in outlying areas.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'Multiple ATMs and banks in town.', 'Nepali | Bhutia | Hindi | English widely used.[web:248][web:251]', TRUE, 'Inner Line/Protected Area permits for specific excursions and for foreign nationals in many parts of Sikkim.[web:248][web:249][web:252]', 'Blend of Lepcha, Bhutia and Nepali influences with strong Buddhist presence.', 'Losar, Saga Dawa and other Buddhist festivals, plus pan-Indian celebrations.', 'Dress modestly for monastery visits and maintain silence inside prayer halls.', 'Handicrafts from Sikkim and North East | Tea and organic products | Buddhist artefacts and souvenirs', 'Thukpa and momos | Gundruk-based dishes | Local teas and bakery items', '{"accommodation_range": [900, 2200], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [300, 800], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [1750, 4200]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2200, 5000], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [700, 1600], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [3700, 8400]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [5000, 18000], "food_range": [800, 2000], "activities_range": [1200, 2500], "local_transport_range": [600, 1400], "total_daily_range": [7600, 23900]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Gangtok & East Sikkim in Sikkim.', 'Appreciated as a clean, tourist-friendly capital that feels less chaotic than many hill towns and works well as a base.[web:248][web:251]', 'Improved road and air connectivity plus increased promotion of Khangchendzonga National Park as India’s only mixed UNESCO site.[web:249][web:252]', 'Follow local rules on plastic use and respect fragile Himalayan slopes when taking short hikes.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-66', 'North Sikkim (Lachung–Lachen Belt)', 'IN-SK', 'north-sikkim', 'North Sikkim', 'North East India', 27.7, 88.71, 2700, 7.0, 'Difficult', '{"name": "Bagdogra / Pakyong (via Gangtok)", "distance_km": 200}'::jsonb, '{"name": "New Jalpaiguri (via Gangtok)", "distance_km": 210}'::jsonb, 'Gangtok', 120.0, 'Narrow mountain roads from Gangtok with landslide-prone sections; only authorised vehicles with permits allowed for tourists.[web:248][web:251]', '{"High_mountain","Valley_scenery","Snow_views","Offbeat"}', '{"Yumthang Valley (‘Valley of Flowers’ in season)","Gurudongmar Lake (high altitude, permits needed)","Lachung and Lachen villages","Hot springs and snow viewpoints (seasonal)"}', '{"Scenic drives and short walks","Valley and snowfield photography","Local homestay experiences"}', 'High-altitude valleys with dramatic landscapes, rhododendron blooms in season and glimpses of Himalayan peaks, accessed via staged overnight trips.[web:248][web:251][web:249][web:252]', 'Quiet homestay lanes away from main hotel clusters | Less-touristed rhododendron patches depending on bloom', 'Spring (April–June) for blooms; autumn and early winter for clearer views.[web:248][web:251]', 'Peak monsoon (landslides, closures) and severe winter spells when access to Gurudongmar/Yumthang can be cut off.', 'April–June (flower season) and October holiday weeks.[web:248][web:251]', 'Monsoon and harshest winter weeks', '{"winter": "-5-8\u00b0C", "summer": "4-16\u00b0C", "monsoon": "6-14\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Heavy; roads frequently affected in rainy periods.[web:248]', '{"Scenery_seekers","Snow_and_high_altitude_lovers","Photographers"}', '{"Scenery_seekers": "Valleys, rivers and mountain backdrops on multi-day drives.[web:248][web:251]", "Snow_and_high_altitude_lovers": "Seasonal snowfields and high lakes like Gurudongmar (subject to health and permits).[web:251]"}'::jsonb, 'Permits compulsory; acclimatisation and health screening important for high-altitude segments; not ideal for travelers with serious heart/respiratory issues.[web:248][web:251]', 2.0, 3.0, 4, 'Typical 2N/3D package: Gangtok–Lachung (night)–Yumthang and back; for Lachen/Gurudongmar add extra night and day.[web:248][web:251]', 'Basic hotels | Homestays | Guesthouses', 'Simple set meals at lodges/homestays; mostly Indian and local hill dishes.', 7.0, 'Altitude, cold and road conditions are the main risks; heed local and army advisories.', 'Very limited; assume low/no mobile data in many stretches.', 'Patchy BSNL; others often absent.', 'ATMs mainly in Gangtok; carry cash for North Sikkim.[web:248]', 'Nepali | Bhutia | Hindi | Basic English in tourism.[web:251]', TRUE, 'Special permits via registered tour operators; foreign nationals have more restrictions near border belts.[web:248][web:249][web:252]', 'Highland Buddhist and rural Sikkimese communities.', 'Local monastery festivals; tourism is more seasonal than event-centric.', 'Respect army presence and photography restrictions near border/strategic areas.', 'Limited; small local products like woollens or snacks', 'Thukpa and momos | Simple rice and curry sets at homestays', '{"accommodation_range": [1200, 2500], "food_range": [300, 600], "activities_range": [400, 1000], "local_transport_range": [600, 1200], "total_daily_range": [2500, 5300]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2500, 4500], "food_range": [500, 900], "activities_range": [800, 1600], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [4600, 8500]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4500, 10000], "food_range": [800, 1800], "activities_range": [1200, 2500], "local_transport_range": [1200, 2200], "total_daily_range": [7700, 16500]}'::jsonb, 'Experience North Sikkim (Lachung–Lachen Belt) in Sikkim.', 'Described as stunning but demanding; many consider it a must-see if comfortable with long, rough drives and basic stays.[web:248][web:251]', 'More regulated tour operations and emphasis on safety/permit compliance.[web:248]', 'High-altitude ecosystems are fragile; never litter, avoid trampling vegetation and follow instructions strictly.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-67', 'Meghalaya (Shillong–Cherrapunji–Mawlynnong circuit)', 'IN-ML', 'east-khasi-hills-and-surroundings', 'East Khasi Hills and surroundings', 'North East India', 25.58, 91.88, 1500, 8.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Shillong (Umroi, limited) / Guwahati", "distance_km": 120}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Guwahati", "distance_km": 100}'::jsonb, 'Guwahati', 100.0, 'Good highways from Guwahati to Shillong and on to Sohra (Cherrapunji) and Dawki; shared cabs and taxis widely used.[web:248][web:251]', '{"Waterfalls","Caves","Living_root_bridges","Family","Adventure"}', '{"Shillong city viewpoints and cafes","Sohra waterfalls (Nohkalikai, Seven Sisters, etc.)","Living root bridges near Nongriat and other villages","Mawlynnong ‘cleanest village’ and Dawki river"}', '{"Waterfall viewing and short hikes","Root-bridge treks (moderate difficulty)","Boating on Umngot River at Dawki (seasonal clarity)","Cave exploration with local guides"}', 'Cloud-laced cliffs, intense waterfalls and indigenous Khasi engineering in the living root bridges, plus glassy rivers in season.[web:248][web:251]', 'Quieter villages and root bridges beyond most visited spots | Lesser-known viewpoints and short trails near Sohra', 'October–April; post-monsoon brings full waterfalls with safer access, winter offers clearer skies.[web:248][web:251]', 'Heaviest monsoon months for landslides and dangerous waterfall conditions; some caves/rivers swell dangerously.', 'Winter holidays and March–April shoulder season.[web:248][web:251]', 'Monsoon for mainstream tourists (though some enthusiasts visit for raw rain experience)', '{"winter": "6-18\u00b0C", "summer": "15-24\u00b0C", "monsoon": "14-22\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Among world’s wettest zones around Sohra/Mawsynram; rainfall shapes entire tourism pattern.[web:248]', '{"Waterfall_and_nature_lovers","Active_travellers","Families_with_older_kids"}', '{"Waterfall_and_nature_lovers": "Multiple falls, green cliffs and root bridges in compact region.[web:248][web:251]", "Active_travellers": "Root-bridge and cave walks require reasonable fitness."}'::jsonb, 'Steep steps on root-bridge trails; always follow local safety instructions at waterfalls and caves.[web:248][web:251]', 3.0, 4.0, 6, 'Day 1: Guwahati–Shillong; Day 2–3: Sohra waterfalls and root bridges; Day 4+: Dawki/Mawlynnong and extra village stays.[web:248][web:251]', 'Shillong hotels and guesthouses | Homestays and small resorts around Sohra and Mawlynnong', 'Mix of Khasi cuisine, North Indian and cafe food; pork and local specialties for non-vegetarians.', 8.0, 'Slippery rocks and high cliffs require caution; region is otherwise welcoming and safe.', 'Good in Shillong; patchy in interior villages but improving.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in Shillong and main towns; limited in smaller villages.', 'Khasi | English widely | Hindi understood in tourism.[web:248][web:251]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Khasi matrilineal communities with strong village councils and church presence.', 'Local religious and harvest festivals; Christmas season is festive across Meghalaya.', 'Obey village rules for trekking routes and photograph people only with consent.', 'Hand-woven shawls and local crafts | Spices and pickles | Bamboo and cane products', 'Jadoh (rice and meat dish) | Smoked meats and local chutneys | Shillong street and cafe food', '{"accommodation_range": [900, 2200], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [300, 800], "local_transport_range": [300, 800], "total_daily_range": [1750, 4300]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2200, 5000], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [700, 1500], "local_transport_range": [500, 1200], "total_daily_range": [3800, 8600]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [5000, 15000], "food_range": [800, 2000], "activities_range": [1200, 2500], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [7800, 21000]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Meghalaya (Shillong–Cherrapunji–Mawlynnong circuit) in Meghalaya.', 'Frequently highlighted for dramatic scenery and unique root bridges; some mention crowding at top spots but many quiet corners remain.[web:248][web:251]', 'More homestays and regulated trekking routes to manage increasing tourist numbers.[web:248]', 'Stick to designated paths, carry back trash and respect local capacity limits on popular trails.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-68', 'Kaziranga National Park & Assam Tea Belt', 'IN-AS', 'golaghat-nagaon-sonitpur', 'Golaghat / Nagaon / Sonitpur', 'North East India', 26.58, 93.17, 80, 8.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Guwahati Airport / Jorhat Airport", "distance_km": 200}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Furkating / Guwahati", "distance_km": 75}'::jsonb, 'Guwahati', 200.0, 'NH27 and other highways link Guwahati and upper Assam to Kaziranga; good road conditions outside flood events.[web:248][web:251][web:249][web:252]', '{"Wildlife","Tea_estates","Family","Photography"}', '{"Kaziranga National Park jeep safaris","One-horned rhinoceros sightings","Elephant-back safaris (limited, regulated)","Tea estate drives and visits in surrounding belt"}', '{"Morning and afternoon safaris in different ranges","Birding","Village and tea-garden visits"}', 'UNESCO-listed floodplain ecosystem famous for its rhino population alongside elephants, deer and rich birdlife, often combined with Assam tea-garden stays.[web:248][web:249][web:252]', 'Less-visited safari ranges with fewer vehicles | Small, charming tea bungalows near park buffers', 'November–April, with pleasant winter temperatures and good sightings.[web:248][web:251]', 'Monsoon (park closed typically from May/June to October due to Brahmaputra floods).[web:248][web:249][web:252]', 'December–February and long weekends.[web:248][web:251]', 'Early/late shoulder around opening/closing months', '{"winter": "8-24\u00b0C", "summer": "24-35\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-30\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Heavy monsoon rains cause seasonal flooding, crucial to ecology but limiting access.[web:249][web:252]', '{"Wildlife_enthusiasts","Families","Tea_and_nature_lovers"}', '{"Wildlife_enthusiasts": "High chances of rhino sightings and diverse fauna.[web:249][web:252]", "Tea_and_nature_lovers": "Combination of park safaris and green tea estates is distinctive.[web:248][web:251]"}'::jsonb, 'Park rules and safari permits need to be followed; some ranges may close temporarily depending on water levels.', 2.0, 3.0, 4, '2–4 safaris over 2–3 days in different ranges plus one relaxed day in a tea estate or village visit.[web:248][web:251]', 'Jungle lodges and resorts | Tea estate bungalows | Budget hotels on highway', 'Lodge buffets with Assamese and Indian dishes; simple fare in nearby towns.', 9.0, 'Very safe if park and guide instructions are respected; do not attempt to walk into core areas.', 'Lodge Wi‑Fi and basic mobile data near highway; weaker deeper inside greenery.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in nearby towns and along main highway.', 'Assamese | Bengali | Hindi | English in tourism.[web:248][web:251]', TRUE, 'Safari permits and range allocations managed by forest department; bookings via lodges and agents.[web:249][web:252]', 'Assamese villages with strong tea-industry presence and Brahmaputra floodplain lifestyle.', 'Bihu festivals in Assam; some lodges offer cultural evenings.', 'Respect local village customs and dress modestly in rural areas.', 'Assam tea directly from estates | Local crafts and woven items', 'Assamese thali with fish or meat | Pitha and local sweets | Freshly brewed Assam tea', '{"accommodation_range": [1500, 3000], "food_range": [400, 800], "activities_range": [1500, 2500], "local_transport_range": [600, 1200], "total_daily_range": [4000, 7500]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3000, 6000], "food_range": [800, 1500], "activities_range": [2500, 3500], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [7100, 13500]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [6000, 15000], "food_range": [1200, 2500], "activities_range": [3500, 6000], "local_transport_range": [1200, 2000], "total_daily_range": [11900, 25500]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Kaziranga National Park & Assam Tea Belt in Assam.', 'Often recommended as India’s top rhino-watching destination with good infrastructure and memorable safaris.[web:248][web:251]', 'Continued conservation successes and eco-tourism focus within UNESCO framework.[web:249][web:252]', 'Choose responsible lodges, minimise noise on safaris and never pressure guides to go off-route.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
