t quieter travel.', 'Peak summer afternoons for temple visits; monsoon when park access and river levels fluctuate.', 'Winter months and around festival/holiday periods.', 'Hot summer and some monsoon weeks', '{"winter": "8-24\u00b0C", "summer": "26-42\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Central Indian monsoon with heavy but seasonal rains.', '{"History_and_architecture_lovers","Wildlife_and_birders","Photographers"}', '{"History_and_architecture_lovers": "Intricate temple sculptures and UNESCO recognition.[web:249][web:252]", "Wildlife_and_birders": "Panna offers tiger, vulture and riverine wildlife viewing."}'::jsonb, 'Respect temple decorum; Panna safari permits should be booked in advance during peak season.', 2.0, 3.0, 4, 'Day 1: Khajuraho Western Group and sound-and-light show; Day 2: Panna safari and Ken River; Day 3: Other temples and relaxed village visit.', 'Hotels near temple complex | Jungle lodges near Panna | Budget guesthouses', 'Indian restaurants and hotel dining; simple options near park gate.', 9.0, 'Tourism-oriented town and park; standard precautions adequate.', 'Good in Khajuraho; patchy nearer park interior.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in Khajuraho town and nearby urban centres.', 'Hindi | Bundeli dialects | English in tourism.[web:249][web:252]', TRUE, 'Safari permits for Panna ranges; temple visits need only entry tickets.', 'Bundelkhand region with mix of rural communities and temple-town economy.', 'Khajuraho Dance Festival and religious festivals enliven temple precincts.', 'Dress modestly in temple areas; remove footwear where required.', 'Stone and brass souvenirs | Local handicrafts and textiles', 'Simple MP-style thalis | Local sweets from small shops', '{"accommodation_range": [900, 2200], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [300, 800], "total_daily_range": [1850, 4400]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2200, 5000], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [800, 1600], "local_transport_range": [500, 1200], "total_daily_range": [3900, 8700]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [5000, 15000], "food_range": [800, 2000], "activities_range": [1500, 3000], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [8100, 21500]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Khajuraho & Panna National Park in Madhya Pradesh.', 'Praised for combining culture and nature; many find 2–3 days sufficient but rewarding.', 'Steady growth in safari tourism at Panna alongside conservation success stories.[web:249][web:252]', 'Follow park rules, avoid graffiti at temples and support local guides and artisans.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-70', 'Orchha & Nearby Betwa Landscapes', 'IN-MP', 'niwari', 'Niwari', 'Central India', 25.35, 78.64, 214, 6.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Gwalior Airport / Khajuraho (farther)", "distance_km": 120}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Jhansi Junction", "distance_km": 18}'::jsonb, 'Jhansi', 18.0, 'Short drive from Jhansi via good roads; well linked to Gwalior, Khajuraho and other Bundelkhand routes.', '{"Heritage","Riverside","Photography","Short_break"}', '{"Orchha Fort complex and palaces","Chhatris (cenotaphs) along Betwa River","Ram Raja Temple and local markets","Betwa riverside scenery and rafting (seasonal, regulated)"}', '{"Fort and temple sightseeing","Sunset photography near chhatris","Short walks and easy cycling","Seasonal light adventure on river"}', 'Compact heritage town with palaces and riverside cenotaphs that feel quieter and less commercial than many big-name sites.', 'Viewpoints across Betwa with skyline of chhatris | Less-visited small temples and village lanes', 'October–March for pleasant days and comfortable walks.', 'Peak summer heat in afternoons; monsoon high river levels for certain water activities.', 'Winter, especially around long weekends and festivals.', 'Summer and mid-monsoon periods', '{"winter": "8-24\u00b0C", "summer": "28-44\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Monsoon rains can swell Betwa and make banks slippery.', '{"History_buffs","Photographers","Slow_travellers"}', '{"History_buffs": "Well-preserved Bundela-era architecture and temples.[web:249][web:252]", "Slow_travellers": "Walkable town with relaxed vibe and scenic riverside."}'::jsonb, 'Smaller town with limited nightlife; river safety should be respected, especially with children.', 1.0, 2.0, 3, 'Day 1: Fort, temples and sunset at chhatris; Day 2: Riverside walks, village exploration and optional rafting in season.', 'Heritage hotels | Guesthouses | Budget lodges', 'Simple local restaurants and hotel dining, mainly Indian cuisine.', 9.0, 'Generally peaceful; main caution is near riverbanks and after dark in very quiet areas.', 'Decent 4G coverage in town.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in Orchha and nearby Jhansi.', 'Hindi | Bundeli dialects | Basic English in tourism.[web:249][web:252]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Religious and heritage town with strong Ram devotion and Bundelkhand traditions.', 'Ram-related festivals draw pilgrims; light-and-sound shows and cultural programmes sometimes held at fort.', 'Dress modestly at temples; evenings near Ram Raja Temple can be quite devotional.', 'Small handicrafts and souvenirs | Local sweets and snacks', 'Street-side chai and snacks by the market | Simple veg thali at dhabas', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 2000], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [200, 700], "local_transport_range": [200, 600], "total_daily_range": [1450, 3800]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2000, 4500], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [500, 1200], "local_transport_range": [400, 800], "total_daily_range": [3300, 7400]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4500, 12000], "food_range": [800, 2000], "activities_range": [800, 1800], "local_transport_range": [500, 1200], "total_daily_range": [6600, 17000]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Orchha & Nearby Betwa Landscapes in Madhya Pradesh.', 'Often called an underrated gem of MP for its tranquil heritage atmosphere and picturesque riverside.', 'Inclusion in more MP heritage circuits along with Gwalior, Jhansi and Khajuraho.[web:249][web:252]', 'Support small local businesses, keep monuments and riverbanks litter-free and respect quiet, small-town rhythm.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-72', 'Almora & Kasar Devi Belt', 'IN-UT', 'almora', 'Almora', 'North India', 29.62, 79.67, 1650, 7.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Pantnagar Airport", "distance_km": 120}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Kathgodam", "distance_km": 90}'::jsonb, 'Haldwani', 95.0, 'Hill roads from Kathgodam/Haldwani with regular buses and shared cabs; Almora is a key hub for nearby valleys like Binsar and Kasar Devi.[web:256]', '{"Hill_town","Culture","Slow_travel","Spiritual"}', '{"Old Almora bazaars and traditional houses","Kasar Devi Temple ridge","Views towards Nanda Devi range on clear days","Proximity to Binsar Wildlife Sanctuary"}', '{"Town and bazaar walks","Ridge walks around Kasar Devi","Short drives to viewpoints and Binsar gate"}', 'Relaxed Kumaon hill town with a historic bazaar core and a ridge (Kasar Devi) long associated with writers, seekers and spiritual travellers.[web:256]', 'Quiet village homestays above/below main ridge | Sunrise and sunset points near Kasar Devi away from crowds', 'October–April for crisp views; monsoon for lush valleys if okay with cloud.[web:256][web:259]', 'Peak monsoon landslide alerts and coldest snaps if not prepared for low temperatures.[web:259]', 'Autumn and winter, particularly November–January.[web:256][web:259]', 'Mid-monsoon and shoulder periods when some cafes shut', '{"winter": "2-14\u00b0C", "summer": "16-28\u00b0C", "monsoon": "14-22\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Typical mid-Himalayan monsoon with some road disruption on very heavy days.', '{"Writers_and_remote_workers","Spiritual_seekers","Budget_backpackers"}', '{"Writers_and_remote_workers": "Quiet guesthouses and cafes on Kasar ridge; many advertise Wi\u2011Fi and long-stay tariffs.[web:256]", "Spiritual_seekers": "Kasar Devi considered an energy spot, mentioned in travel and spiritual circuits.[web:256]"}'::jsonb, 'Nights can be cold; some guesthouses basic; carry cash as digital payments may fail during network dips.', 2.0, 3.0, 6, 'Use Almora/Kasar as a base: mix slow days on ridge and bazaar walks with a day-trip into Binsar or nearby villages.[web:256]', 'Budget lodges in Almora | Cafes-with-rooms at Kasar Devi | Homestays and small resorts on surrounding hills', 'Simple Kumaoni and North Indian food plus traveller cafes on ridge serving basics and coffee.[web:256]', 8.0, 'Generally safe; typical hill-road caution applies for drives to/from town.', '4G in town; variable along ridge and interiors but many cafes provide workable Wi‑Fi.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi (spotty in some higher pockets)', 'ATMs in Almora town; none on remote ridges.', 'Hindi | Kumaoni | Basic English in tourism.[web:256]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Traditional Kumaoni families, temples and old bazaar traditions mixed with newer alternative/creative communities.', 'Local temple fairs and standard hill festivals; occasional retreats/workshops around Kasar.', 'Dress modestly near temples and in old-town lanes; support local shops for snacks and essentials.', 'Kumaoni sweets like bal mithai and singauri | Local woollens and shawls | Village-made pickles and pulses', 'Bhatt ki churkani and other Kumaoni dals | Bal mithai and singauri | Simple homely thalis', '{"accommodation_range": [700, 1600], "food_range": [200, 450], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [200, 500], "total_daily_range": [1300, 3150]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1600, 3500], "food_range": [350, 800], "activities_range": [400, 1000], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [2650, 6050]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3500, 10000], "food_range": [700, 1500], "activities_range": [800, 1800], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [5400, 14200]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Almora & Kasar Devi Belt in Uttarakhand.', 'Perceived as a calm, culturally rich base close to Binsar; many mention Kasar’s vibe as particularly conducive to reflection.[web:256]', 'Slow-travel and wellness-oriented stays increasingly promoted around Kasar ridge.[web:256]', 'Water is limited; use sparingly and avoid plastic—hill towns struggle with solid waste management.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-75', 'Jibhi & Tirthan Valley', 'IN-HP', 'kullu', 'Kullu', 'North India', 31.61, 77.3, 1600, 8.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Kullu (Bhuntar) Airport", "distance_km": 50}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Chandigarh", "distance_km": 250}'::jsonb, 'Chandigarh', 250.0, 'Road from Aut tunnel on Chandigarh–Manali highway into Tirthan and Jibhi region; regular buses to Aut, then local taxis.[web:257]', '{"Offbeat_hill","Riverside","Backpacking","Slow_travel"}', '{"Riverside villages along Tirthan River","Wooden homestays in Jibhi and Shoja","Easy access to Great Himalayan National Park region (GHNP gate)"}', '{"Village and forest walks","Short treks to waterfalls and viewpoints","Riverside camping and bonfires (in season)"}', 'Peaceful valley with cedar forests, wooden homes and riverside stays, popular among backpackers escaping Manali crowds.[web:257][web:260]', 'Smaller hamlets beyond main Jibhi market | Offbeat stays nearer GHNP entry', 'March–June and September–November for pleasant weather; winter for snow in higher reaches.[web:257]', 'Days of heavy monsoon landslides and peak winter road closures around Jalori and high passes.[web:257]', 'April–June and autumn long weekends.[web:257]', 'Mid-monsoon (except for slow travellers okay with storms)', '{"winter": "0-12\u00b0C", "summer": "12-26\u00b0C", "monsoon": "10-22\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Himalayan monsoon with swelling streams and lush forests.[web:257]', '{"Backpackers","Couples","Remote_workers"}', '{"Backpackers": "Budget-friendly hostels and homestays, easy trails and social bonfire evenings.[web:257]", "Remote_workers": "Workation stays overlooking river and forest, especially in shoulder seasons."}'::jsonb, 'Area is growing fast; respect village privacy and avoid loud parties; check connectivity if planning remote work.[web:257]', 2.0, 3.0, 7, 'Use Jibhi/Tirthan as a base: mix short hikes, riverside time and day trips to Jalori Pass and GHNP gate over 3–5 days.[web:257]', 'Homestays | Backpacker hostels | Riverside cottages', 'Homely Himachali food and simple cafes serving Indian and continental dishes.', 8.0, 'Stream currents and slippery forest paths in monsoon demand care; otherwise low crime.', 'Improving 4G; many stays advertise workable Wi‑Fi, but speeds vary by village.[web:257]', 'Jio | Airtel (better near main roads) | Vi limited', 'ATMs at Aut/Banjar; limited in deeper villages.', 'Hindi | Himachali dialects | Basic English in tourism.[web:257]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Himachali villages with agriculture, orchards and small-scale tourism.', 'Local fairs and temple festivals; valley retains traditional rhythms.', 'Ask before entering fields or photographing homes; keep music volume low at night.', 'Handmade woollens and local produce | Honey and jams from homestays', 'Siddu and other Himachali dishes | Local rajma (kidney beans) preparations', '{"accommodation_range": [700, 1600], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [1450, 3400]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1600, 3500], "food_range": [400, 800], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [2800, 6100]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3500, 9000], "food_range": [700, 1500], "activities_range": [800, 1800], "local_transport_range": [500, 1000], "total_daily_range": [5500, 13300]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Jibhi & Tirthan Valley in Himachal Pradesh.', 'Highly rated by backpackers for serenity and affordability; many consider it their favourite alternative to Manali.[web:257]', 'Rise in boutique cabins and hostels; GHNP being promoted for soft eco-tourism.[web:257]', 'Valley is sensitive; avoid plastic, stick to marked paths and support homestays that manage waste responsibly.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-76', 'Chitkul & Baspa Valley', 'IN-HP', 'kinnaur', 'Kinnaur', 'North India', 31.35, 78.43, 3450, 7.0, 'Difficult', '{"name": "Shimla / Kullu (Bhuntar)", "distance_km": 250}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Shimla (narrow gauge) / Kalka", "distance_km": 240}'::jsonb, 'Shimla', 230.0, 'Long Himalayan drive via Shimla–Rampur–Sangla–Chitkul; roads narrow and landslide-prone in sections.[web:257]', '{"High_mountain_village","Offbeat","Road_trip","Photography"}', '{"Chitkul village on Baspa River","Valley meadows and pine forests","‘Last village’ feel near Indo–Tibetan border"}', '{"Village walks and riverside strolls","Short hikes to meadows","Photography of peaks and traditional houses"}', 'End-of-the-road village with stone-and-wood houses, roaring river and close snow peaks, often cited as among Himachal’s prettiest settlements.[web:257]', 'Homestays slightly away from main road | Low-key trails along river and fields', 'May–October (excluding peak monsoon) for access and green or post-monsoon views.[web:257][web:259]', 'Deep winter for heavy snow and road closures; peak monsoon for landslides.[web:259]', 'May–June and September holiday weeks.[web:257]', 'Early spring and late autumn with fewer visitors but colder nights', '{"winter": "-10-6\u00b0C", "summer": "4-18\u00b0C", "monsoon": "6-16\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Moderate precipitation; heavy snow in winter and snow/rain mix in shoulder months.', '{"Scenery_lovers","Photographers","Quiet_seekers"}', '{"Scenery_lovers": "Baspa valley is consistently praised for river, forest and snow-peak combination.[web:257]", "Quiet_seekers": "Remote location with limited nightlife and simple routines."}'::jsonb, 'Altitude sensitivity, limited medical facilities and long drive time; carry warm layers even in summer.', 2.0, 2.0, 4, 'Part of Kinnaur loop: Kalpa/Sangla–Chitkul 1–2 nights, then onward or back to Shimla.[web:257]', 'Guesthouses | Homestays | Simple hotels', 'Basic Himachali/North Indian set meals at lodges and dhabas.', 7.0, 'Road edges and weather are primary risks; avoid night driving and stay updated on road conditions.[web:257]', 'Very limited; assume low or no mobile data.', 'Patchy BSNL; other networks spotty or absent.', 'ATMs in bigger towns like Sangla/Recong Peo; none in Chitkul.', 'Hindi | Kinnauri dialects | Basic English at tourist lodges.[web:257]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Kinnauri communities with distinct architecture and temples.', 'Local village festivals at temples; seasons drive activity more than big events.', 'Respect temple areas and avoid entering fields without consent.', 'Small local woollens or souvenirs | Simple snacks and local produce', 'Rajma-chawal with local beans | Simple homely curries', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 1800], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [200, 500], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [1650, 3700]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1800, 3500], "food_range": [400, 800], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [600, 1200], "total_daily_range": [3200, 6400]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3500, 9000], "food_range": [700, 1500], "activities_range": [700, 1800], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [5700, 21800]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Chitkul & Baspa Valley in Himachal Pradesh.', 'Often called a dream ‘last village’ experience, praised for air quality and views; some feel access roads can be tiring.[web:257][web:259]', 'More guesthouses and camps have opened; authorities highlight need for responsible tourism.[web:257]', 'Carry back waste, avoid disturbing riverbanks and forests, and choose smaller homestays over large intrusive constructions.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-77', 'Miyar Valley', 'IN-HP', 'lahaul-and-pangi-region', 'Lahaul and Pangi region', 'North India', 32.87, 76.95, 3600, 5.0, 'Difficult', '{"name": "Kullu (Bhuntar) / Leh (farther)", "distance_km": 250}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Joginder Nagar / Chandigarh", "distance_km": 300}'::jsonb, 'Manali (gateway)', 180.0, 'Accessed via Manali–Rohtang/Atal Tunnel into Lahaul and then side roads/jeep tracks; limited public transport, often arranged via trek operators.[web:260]', '{"Trekking","High_altitude_valley","Offbeat","Adventure"}', '{"Long glacial valley between Pir Panjal and Zanskar ranges","Remote villages and meadows","Base for trekking and climbing expeditions"}', '{"Multi-day treks and camping","High-altitude photography","Exploration of side valleys with guides"}', 'Remote valley that combines elements of Himachal and Ladakh landscapes, still far less visited than popular Himalayan circuits.[web:260]', 'Wildflower-filled meadows in summer | Tiny hamlets with very basic homestays', 'July–September for trekking and open-valley access.[web:260]', 'Winter and shoulder seasons when snow blocks routes; monsoon storms can still affect approach roads.', 'Short Himalayan summer; crowding is limited due to remoteness.[web:260]', 'Most of the year outside core season', '{"winter": "-18--2\u00b0C", "summer": "0-18\u00b0C", "monsoon": "2-16\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Lies in rain-shadow-like conditions but approaches can see rain/snow; weather changeable.[web:260]', '{"Experienced_trekkers","Expedition_photographers","Offbeat_explorers"}', '{"Experienced_trekkers": "Long valley treks without huge technical difficulty but with remote conditions.[web:260]", "Offbeat_explorers": "One of the less-commercialised high valleys, offering real wilderness."}'::jsonb, 'Should only be attempted with proper gear, guides and acclimatisation; emergency services sparse.', 5.0, 7.0, 10, 'Usually planned as a 5–9 day trek from Udaipur/nearby access villages into valley and back with camping.[web:260]', 'Homestays in approach villages | Tented camps on treks', 'Basic; trek kitchens and homestay meals based on local staples.', 6.0, 'Remoteness, altitude and weather demands serious preparation; not suited for casual tourists.[web:260]', 'Minimal to none once inside valley.', 'Patchy or absent; some signal closer to bigger approach points.', 'ATMs only in larger towns before entering valley region.', 'Hindi | Local Lahauli dialects | Basic English with some guides.[web:260]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Sparse high-altitude communities with mixed Himalayan influences.', 'Local village festivities; valley primarily a trekker’s destination.', 'Travel respectfully; homestays may have very simple facilities—adjust expectations.', 'None inside valley; supplies must be pre-arranged', 'Simple lentil–rice meals | Local breads when available', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 1800], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [400, 1200], "local_transport_range": [500, 1200], "total_daily_range": [1950, 4700]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1800, 3500], "food_range": [400, 800], "activities_range": [800, 1800], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [3800, 7600]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3500, 9000], "food_range": [700, 1500], "activities_range": [1500, 3000], "local_transport_range": [1000, 2000], "total_daily_range": [6700, 15500]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Miyar Valley in Himachal Pradesh.', 'Celebrated among niche trekking and climbing communities; often described as pristine and unspoilt.[web:260]', 'Highlighted in lists of truly unexplored Himachal valleys; still kept low-key in mainstream tourism.[web:260]', 'Absolutely pack-in–pack-out for all waste; avoid campfires and follow Leave No Trace principles strictly.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-78', 'Keoladeo National Park (Bharatpur Bird Sanctuary)', 'IN-RJ', 'bharatpur', 'Bharatpur', 'North India', 27.16, 77.52, 180, 9.0, 'Easy', '{"name": "Agra Airport / Delhi Airport (farther)", "distance_km": 55}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Bharatpur Junction", "distance_km": 5}'::jsonb, 'Agra', 55.0, 'Just off the Delhi–Agra–Jaipur Golden Triangle highways; easy access by car, bus and train.[web:258][web:261]', '{"Birding","Wetland","Photography","Short_break"}', '{"Wetland and woodland habitat with hundreds of bird species","Winter migratory birds including cranes and ducks","Well-laid cycle/foot paths inside park"}', '{"Birdwatching by cycle, on foot or cycle-rickshaw","Guided naturalist tours","Nature photography"}', 'Compact UNESCO-listed bird sanctuary offering close, easy bird views in a semi-arid landscape turned wetland oasis.[web:258][web:261][web:249][web:252]', 'Early-morning and late-evening walks with fewer visitors | Inner tracks where mammals like nilgai and jackal may be seen', 'October–March for winter migrants, with peak diversity in mid-winter.[web:258][web:261]', 'Peak summer heat and mid-monsoon when bird numbers and comfort drop.', 'December–February weekends and holidays.[web:258][web:261]', 'Summer months; monsoon is quieter though some residents remain', '{"winter": "5-22\u00b0C", "summer": "26-42\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Seasonal monsoon regenerates wetlands; water levels crucial to bird life.[web:258]', '{"Birders","Families","Photographers","School_groups"}', '{"Birders": "One of Asia\u2019s finest birding sites with rich species diversity.[web:258][web:261]", "Families": "Flat paths and cycle-rickshaws make it accessible for all ages.[web:258]"}'::jsonb, 'Park entry fees plus separate charges for rickshaws/guides; best visited early or late in day for birds and soft light.[web:258]', 1.0, 2.0, 3, 'Combine 1–2 mornings/evenings in park with a Golden Triangle trip including Agra and Jaipur.[web:258][web:261]', 'Hotels and lodges near park gate | Budget guesthouses in Bharatpur town', 'Hotel restaurants and local dhabas; simple North Indian and Rajasthani fare.', 9.0, 'Very safe; main caution is sun exposure and hydration.', 'Good 4G near town and lodges; less reliable deeper in park.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in Bharatpur town.', 'Hindi | Rajasthani dialects | English with guides.[web:258]', TRUE, 'Entry tickets at gate; no special permits needed for most Indians and foreign tourists beyond fee payment.[web:258]', 'Small-town Rajasthan with agriculture around wetland.', 'Birding festivals and events occasionally organised; best experiences revolve around migration season.', 'Respect park rules, keep noise low and stay on designated paths.', 'Basic bird and wildlife souvenirs | Local snacks in nearby markets', 'Rajasthani-style thali at dhabas | Local sweets from town', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 2000], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [200, 600], "total_daily_range": [1650, 4000]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2000, 4500], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [800, 1500], "local_transport_range": [300, 800], "total_daily_range": [3500, 7700]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4500, 12000], "food_range": [800, 2000], "activities_range": [1200, 2500], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [6900, 17400]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Keoladeo National Park (Bharatpur Bird Sanctuary) in Rajasthan.', 'Consistently praised by birders worldwide for density and accessibility of sightings; many include it in top Indian birding lists.[web:258][web:261]', 'Improved conservation and water-management measures; ongoing promotion as prime birding destination for 2025–26.[web:258][web:261]', 'Use binoculars and long lenses instead of approaching birds; avoid litter and support eco-friendly guides and lodges.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-79', 'Ranganathittu Bird Sanctuary', 'IN-KA', 'mandya', 'Mandya', 'South India', 12.42, 76.65, 695, 7.0, 'Easy', '{"name": "Mysuru / Bengaluru", "distance_km": 20}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Srirangapatna / Mysuru", "distance_km": 5}'::jsonb, 'Mysuru', 15.0, 'Just off the Mysuru–Bengaluru highway; easy stop on road trips or day trips from Mysuru.[web:261]', '{"Birding","Wetland","Day_trip","Family"}', '{"River-island sanctuary on Kaveri","Large nesting colonies of storks, ibises and other waterbirds","Short boat rides for close views"}', '{"Boat safaris with guides","Birdwatching from banks","Short walks and picnics"}', 'Compact wetland where breeding waterbirds nest on islets, offering close viewing from boats, ideal for a few hours’ birding.[web:261]', 'Early-morning boat rides with fewer visitors | Off-peak weekday visits during breeding season', 'December–March for peak nesting and bird activity.[web:261]', 'Peak summer afternoons for heat; flood periods when river levels are high.', 'Weekends in winter; combines with Mysuru and Srirangapatna visits.[web:261]', 'Non-breeding months and hot seasons', '{"winter": "16-28\u00b0C", "summer": "22-34\u00b0C", "monsoon": "20-28\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Kaveri-fed wetland with seasonal fluctuations depending on monsoon.', '{"Beginner_birders","Families_with_kids","Road_trippers"}', '{"Beginner_birders": "Easy, short experience with reliable sightings and simple logistics.[web:261]", "Families_with_kids": "Boat rides and visible birds keep children engaged."}'::jsonb, 'Follow lifejacket and boat-safety instructions; do not throw food to birds or into water.[web:261]', 0.5, 0.5, 1, 'Include as a half-day excursion from Mysuru along with Srirangapatna or en route between Bengaluru and Mysuru.[web:261]', 'Day-trip only; stay in nearby Mysuru or highway resorts', 'Basic snacks and nearby eateries; most visitors eat in Mysuru or along highway.', 9.0, 'Very safe; keep distance from river edge and follow staff guidance.', 'Highway and nearby towns have good 4G.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in Srirangapatna and Mysuru.', 'Kannada | Hindi | English with guides.[web:261]', TRUE, 'Entry tickets and separate boat-ride charges; no special permits.', 'Part of Kaveri river landscape near historic Srirangapatna.', 'None specific; birding itself peaks in winter.', 'Respect sanctuary rules and quiet environment.', 'Very limited; basic souvenirs nearby', 'Mysuru-style meals in city after visit', '{"accommodation_range": [0, 0], "food_range": [200, 400], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [300, 600], "total_daily_range": [700, 1600]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [0, 0], "food_range": [300, 600], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [1100, 2400]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [0, 0], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [600, 1200], "local_transport_range": [600, 1000], "total_daily_range": [1600, 3100]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Ranganathittu Bird Sanctuary in Karnataka.', 'Liked as an easy, rewarding birding stop; often recommended in birding lists for South India.[web:261]', 'Renewed attention in 2025 birding-destination roundups as a top short-trip site.[web:261]', 'Avoid loud music, do not disturb nesting birds and keep riverbanks litter-free.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-80', 'Nal Sarovar Bird Sanctuary', 'IN-GJ', 'ahmedabad-surendranagar', 'Ahmedabad / Surendranagar', 'West India', 22.8, 72.05, 60, 7.0, 'Easy', '{"name": "Ahmedabad Airport", "distance_km": 65}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Ahmedabad / Viramgam", "distance_km": 40}'::jsonb, 'Ahmedabad', 60.0, 'Connected by good roads from Ahmedabad; popular as a winter day trip by car or taxi.[web:261]', '{"Wetland","Birding","Day_trip","Photography"}', '{"Vast shallow lake and marshes","Large flocks of winter migratory birds","Boating among islets and bird congregations"}', '{"Boat rides with local boatmen","Birdwatching and photography","Short walks on islets where allowed"}', 'Expansive wetland that transforms into a major winter bird haven with flamingos, pelicans and other waterbirds.[web:261]', 'Early starts to catch sunrise and bird activity before crowd arrival | Exploring slightly farther islets with fewer boats (within regulations)', 'November–February when migratory birds peak and temperatures are pleasant.[web:261]', 'Hot summer and heavy monsoon when bird numbers and comfort decline.', 'Winter weekends and holidays; popular with local families and photographers.[web:261]', 'Non-winter months', '{"winter": "10-26\u00b0C", "summer": "26-42\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Seasonal monsoon fills and refreshes wetland; bird visitors follow water and food cycles.[web:261]', '{"Birdwatchers","Families_from_Ahmedabad","Photographers"}', '{"Birdwatchers": "Listed among top Indian birding wetlands with strong winter diversity.[web:261]", "Families_from_Ahmedabad": "Easy day trip combining boat rides and open-air time."}'::jsonb, 'Arrive early to avoid mid-day glare and crowds; negotiate clear prices and time for boats in advance.[web:261]', 0.5, 0.5, 1, 'Morning departure from Ahmedabad, boat rides and birding till late morning, then return via local eateries.', 'Usually day-trip only; overnight options are in Ahmedabad or small lodges nearby', 'Snack stalls and small eateries; most visitors plan main meals in Ahmedabad or highway dhabas.', 9.0, 'Very safe; ensure lifejackets for children on boats and avoid leaning out.', 'Mobile data available near entry and along approach roads.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in nearby towns and on Ahmedabad side; none inside sanctuary.', 'Gujarati | Hindi | Basic English with some boatmen.[web:261]', TRUE, 'Entry tickets plus separate boating charges; no complex permits.', 'Wetland used traditionally by local communities; many boatmen come from nearby villages.', 'Occasional birding events and nature camps in winter.', 'Use designated entry points and follow sanctuary rules; no loud music.', 'Very limited; focus is nature, not shopping', 'Gujarati snacks and tea at local stalls', '{"accommodation_range": [0, 0], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [1050, 2300]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [0, 0], "food_range": [300, 600], "activities_range": [600, 1200], "local_transport_range": [600, 1200], "total_daily_range": [1500, 3000]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [0, 0], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [900, 1500], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [2100, 3900]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Nal Sarovar Bird Sanctuary in Gujarat.', 'Popular with Gujarat-based birders and photographers; often noted for impressive flamingo and pelican flocks in good years.[web:261]', 'Highlighted in 2025 birding lists as a must-visit wetland in western India.[web:261]', 'Do not request boatmen to chase birds for closer photos; maintain distance and avoid littering in boats or on islets.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-81', 'Great Rann of Kutch (White Desert)', 'IN-GJ', 'kutch', 'Kutch', 'West India', 24.09, 70.64, 15, 9.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Bhuj Airport", "distance_km": 80}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Bhuj", "distance_km": 80}'::jsonb, 'Bhuj', 80.0, 'Good roads from Bhuj to Dhordo and beyond; desert roads are mostly paved with final stretches controlled by border/security checkposts.[web:262][web:264][web:236][web:210][web:267]', '{"Desert","Festival","Culture","Photography"}', '{"Endless white salt desert vistas","Sunset and full-moon views over salt flats","Rann Utsav tent city (seasonal) and cultural shows","Nearby sites like Kala Dungar and handicraft villages"}', '{"Sunset/sunrise walks on salt flats","Cultural performances and handicraft bazaars (during festival)","Camel carts and simple desert activities","Short trips to Mandvi coast and local villages"}', 'One of the world’s largest salt deserts, turning into a shimmering white expanse in the dry season and hosting the colourful Rann Utsav near Dhordo.[web:262][web:264][web:236][web:210][web:267]', 'Quieter stretches of the white desert away from main sunset crowd (within permitted zones) | Small artisan villages in Kutch for textiles and embroidery', 'November–February, coinciding with Rann Utsav and cooler desert weather; full-moon nights are especially striking.[web:264][web:236][web:210][web:267]', 'Peak summer and monsoon when flats are marshy or waterlogged and heat is severe.[web:262][web:264]', 'December–January around festivals, New Year and full-moon event dates.[web:236][web:267]', 'Non-festival months and hotter shoulder periods', '{"winter": "8-26\u00b0C", "summer": "26-44\u00b0C", "monsoon": "26-34\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Arid to semi-arid; monsoon turns the salt desert into a shallow marsh before drying out again.[web:262]', '{"Culture_and_festival_lovers","Landscape_photographers","Families","Couples"}', '{"Culture_and_festival_lovers": "Rann Utsav packages combine folk music, dance, crafts and desert stays in one **immersive** experience.[web:236][web:210][web:267]", "Landscape_photographers": "Vast, minimal white foregrounds with dramatic sunsets and moonlight.[web:264][web:263]"}'::jsonb, 'Border-adjacent region; permits/checkposts apply; nights can be very cold even when days feel warm.[web:262][web:264]', 2.0, 3.0, 4, 'Day 1: Arrive Bhuj–Dhordo; evening at White Rann; Day 2: Kala Dungar and crafts; Day 3: Optional Mandvi beach / extra desert night.[web:210][web:236][web:264]', 'Festival tent city (seasonal packages) | Resorts and camps around Dhordo | Hotels in Bhuj town', 'Gujarati thalis and snacks in camps and local eateries, with simple vegetarian-heavy menus.[web:210][web:236]', 9.0, 'Very safe tourist zone; follow marked areas on the desert and stay clear of restricted border stretches.[web:262]', '4G in Bhuj and patchy but improving near festival zones; camps often provide Wi‑Fi.[web:236]', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi (stronger around Bhuj and main roads)', 'ATMs in Bhuj and larger Kutch towns; carry cash to desert camps.[web:264]', 'Gujarati | Kutchi | Hindi | Basic English in tourism.[web:262][web:264]', TRUE, 'Rann entry permit and ID often checked at Bhirandiyara/Dhordo checkpoints due to proximity to international border.[web:262][web:264]', 'Kutchi communities renowned for textiles, embroidery, folk music and desert pastoral traditions.[web:236][web:210]', 'Rann Utsav (White Desert Festival) typically runs from Nov–Feb with nightly cultural programmes.[web:236][web:210][web:267]', 'Dress modestly in villages, ask before photographing people or crafts, and bargain respectfully.', 'Kutchi embroidery and mirror-work textiles | Handwoven shawls and stoles | Leatherwork and handicrafts from artisan villages', 'Gujarati thali with local farsan | Kutch dabeli and snacks | Traditional bajra rotla with ghee', '{"accommodation_range": [1500, 2800], "food_range": [300, 700], "activities_range": [400, 1000], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [2600, 5400]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2800, 6000], "food_range": [600, 1200], "activities_range": [800, 1800], "local_transport_range": [600, 1200], "total_daily_range": [4800, 10200]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [6000, 20000], "food_range": [1000, 2500], "activities_range": [1500, 3500], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [9300, 27500]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Great Rann of Kutch (White Desert) in Gujarat.', 'Frequently described as surreal and otherworldly; many travellers recommend at least one moonlit night on the white desert.[web:264][web:263][web:236]', 'Well-organised Rann Utsav infrastructure with new tent clusters and curated itineraries for 2025–26.[web:236][web:210][web:267]', 'Stay on designated paths to avoid crust damage, minimise plastic use and support local artisans directly.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-82', 'Jaisalmer & Thar Desert Dunes', 'IN-RJ', 'jaisalmer', 'Jaisalmer', 'North India', 26.91, 70.91, 225, 9.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Jaisalmer Airport (seasonal flights) / Jodhpur", "distance_km": 15}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Jaisalmer", "distance_km": 2}'::jsonb, 'Jodhpur', 280.0, 'Highways link Jaisalmer with Jodhpur, Jaipur and other Rajasthan cities; dunes accessed by smaller roads towards Sam and Khuri.[web:266]', '{"Desert","Heritage","Festival","Photography"}', '{"Living Jaisalmer Fort and havelis","Sam and Khuri sand dunes","Desert camps and cultural evenings","Gadisar Lake and nearby temples"}', '{"Camel and jeep safaris in dunes","Overnight desert camping","Fort and old-town heritage walks"}', 'Golden sandstone fort city at the edge of the Thar, combining intricate havelis with easy access to rolling sand dunes.[web:266]', 'Quieter dunes beyond the most crowded Sam belt | Smaller havelis and lanes away from main bazaar', 'October–March for cool desert evenings and comfortable fort exploration.[web:266]', 'Peak summer heat and hottest pre-monsoon months; occasional dust storms.', 'December–January and around Desert Festival dates, plus long-weekend spikes.[web:266]', 'Summer and mid-monsoon when temperatures are extreme and camps may close', '{"winter": "7-26\u00b0C", "summer": "28-45\u00b0C", "monsoon": "26-36\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Very low rainfall desert climate with occasional intense showers.', '{"First_time_desert_visitors","Couples","Families","History_lovers"}', '{"First_time_desert_visitors": "Classic camel-safari-plus-fort combo on the Desert Circuit promoted nationally.[web:266]", "History_lovers": "Lived-in fort and carved havelis provide rich built heritage."}'::jsonb, 'Choose reputable camps that avoid loud generators and dune degradation; nights can be cold even when days are warm.', 2.0, 3.0, 4, 'Day 1: Fort and old city; Day 2: Desert camp with sunset and cultural show; Day 3: Havelis and free time/shopping.', 'Heritage havelis and hotels | Budget guesthouses in town | Desert camps (ranging from basic to luxury)', 'Rajasthani and North Indian food, with many rooftop eateries overlooking fort and town.', 9.0, 'Tourist-oriented city; typical precautions suffice; watch footing on fort ramps and dunes at night.', 'Good in town; weaker but present at many larger camps.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'Multiple ATMs in Jaisalmer town.', 'Hindi | Rajasthani/Marwari | English in tourism.[web:266]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Rajasthani desert communities with folk music, dance and crafts forming a key part of tourist evenings.', 'Jaisalmer Desert Festival and Rajasthan Desert Circuit promotions draw extra cultural programmes.[web:266]', 'Dress modestly in older quarters and near temples; tipping for musicians and camel handlers is customary.', 'Mirror-work textiles and quilts | Jewellery and handicrafts | Camel leather items (ensure ethical sourcing)', 'Dal baati churma | Ker sangri | Local sweets like ghevar and mawa', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 2000], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [300, 800], "total_daily_range": [1750, 4200]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2000, 4500], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [800, 1500], "local_transport_range": [500, 1200], "total_daily_range": [3700, 8100]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4500, 18000], "food_range": [800, 2000], "activities_range": [1500, 3500], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [7600, 25000]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Jaisalmer & Thar Desert Dunes in Rajasthan.', 'Often cited as a must-visit on Rajasthan’s desert circuit for its fort silhouette and desert stays.', 'Ongoing promotion under Desert Circuit itineraries and upgrades to desert-road infrastructure.[web:266]', 'Avoid driving directly on fragile dune crests, say no to plastic cutlery at camps and support smaller local operators.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-83', 'Maravanthe & Karnataka Offbeat Coast', 'IN-KA', 'udupi', 'Udupi', 'South India', 13.63, 74.69, 5, 6.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Mangaluru Airport", "distance_km": 110}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Kundapura / Byndoor", "distance_km": 25}'::jsonb, 'Udupi / Mangaluru', 55.0, 'NH66 coastal highway runs beside Maravanthe with the sea on one side and river/backwaters on the other, making it an iconic self-drive stretch.[web:265]', '{"Coastal_drive","Offbeat_beach","Slow_travel"}', '{"Maravanthe Beach strip with river on one side, sea on the other","Nearby Kodi Beach and quiet fishing hamlets","Easy extensions to Udupi, Murudeshwar and Gokarna"}', '{"Scenic drives and photo stops","Beach walks and simple village visits","Backwater and boat experiences in nearby areas"}', 'Striking road section where the Arabian Sea and a river run parallel to the highway, plus little-known coves and villages ideal for unhurried stops.[web:265]', 'Kodi Beach near Kundapura for peaceful sunsets | Small homestays away from the main highway', 'November–March for calmer seas and comfortable coastal weather.[web:265]', 'Peak monsoon for high waves and heavy rain; some erosion along highway edges occurs.[web:265]', 'Christmas–New Year and long weekends; still quieter than major resort beaches.[web:265]', 'Most weekdays and shoulder months, especially outside school holidays', '{"winter": "22-32\u00b0C", "summer": "26-35\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-30\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Heavy coastal Karnataka monsoon with strong onshore winds.', '{"Road_trippers","Quiet_beach_lovers","Couples"}', '{"Road_trippers": "Regularly featured as one of India\u2019s most scenic coastal drives.[web:265]", "Quiet_beach_lovers": "Less commercial than big-name beaches; more space for relaxed, **slow** stays.[web:265]"}'::jsonb, 'Sea can be rough; swim only where locals deem it safe; limited nightlife or typical resort entertainment.', 1.0, 2.0, 4, 'Use Maravanthe/Kundapura as a night halt in a Konkan drive, with time for beach walks and village visits.', 'Small resorts and homestays near beach | Highway lodges | Guesthouses in Kundapura/Udupi', 'Coastal Karnataka food with fish curries, ghee roast and simple vegetarian thalis in local eateries.[web:265]', 8.0, 'Highway traffic is fast; take care when stopping for photos and crossing roads.', 'Good 4G along highway and in nearby towns.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in Kundapura and other small towns along highway.', 'Kannada | Tulu | Konkani | Hindi and some English in tourism.[web:265]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Fishing communities and temple towns along the Karavali coast.', 'Temple festivals and annual fairs in nearby towns; not a single-event destination.', 'Dress modestly in villages and near temples; be respectful of fishermen and their working spaces.', 'Local snacks and coastal sweets | Basic handicrafts from nearby towns', 'Fish gassi with neer dosa | Udupi-style vegetarian meals', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 2000], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [1550, 3800]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2000, 4500], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [3200, 7200]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4500, 10000], "food_range": [700, 1500], "activities_range": [600, 1500], "local_transport_range": [500, 1000], "total_daily_range": [6300, 14000]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Maravanthe & Karnataka Offbeat Coast in Karnataka.', 'Frequently praised as a hidden-gem coastal stretch and a highlight on long Konkan road trips.[web:265]', 'Featured in new lists of unexplored beaches and coastal self-drive routes in India.[web:265]', 'Avoid littering highway viewpoints and beaches; support homestays that manage waste sensibly.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-84', 'Astaranga & Ramachandi Beaches (Odisha Quiet Coast)', 'IN-OD', 'puri', 'Puri', 'East India', 19.9, 86.08, 3, 6.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Bhubaneswar Airport", "distance_km": 70}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Puri / Bhubaneswar", "distance_km": 45}'::jsonb, 'Puri', 40.0, 'Reachable by coastal roads branching from Puri–Konark–Bhubaneswar circuit; suited to taxis and self-drives.[web:265][web:268]', '{"Offbeat_beach","Sunset","Culture_combo"}', '{"Astaranga’s colourful sunsets over Bay of Bengal","Ramachandi Beach near Konark","Proximity to Konark Sun Temple and Puri"}', '{"Quiet beach walks and photography","Watching fishing boats and village life","Combining with temple and heritage visits nearby"}', 'Under-the-radar beaches on the Puri–Konark belt, known for vivid sunsets and relatively empty sands compared with main Puri beach.[web:265][web:268]', 'Less-frequented stretches of Astaranga beyond main access points | Morning hours when fishing activity is high but tourists are few', 'November–February for mild weather and calm sea views.[web:265][web:268]', 'Cyclone-prone late-monsoon/post-monsoon periods and very hot April–May afternoons.', 'Around big festivals at Puri plus winter holiday weeks; these beaches still stay quieter than the main town.[web:268]', 'Most non-festival weekdays and sultry pre-monsoon weeks', '{"winter": "16-28\u00b0C", "summer": "28-38\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Coastal monsoon with heavy showers and occasional systems in Bay of Bengal.', '{"Sunset_chasers","Quiet_beach_seekers","Culture_plus_sea_travellers"}', '{"Sunset_chasers": "Astaranga literally means \u2018colourful sunset\u2019 and is noted for evening skies.[web:268]", "Culture_plus_sea_travellers": "Easy to combine sea-time with Konark and Puri temple visits on same trip.[web:265][web:268]"}'::jsonb, 'Limited tourist infrastructure on sand; carry basic supplies and heed local advice on sea conditions.', 1.0, 1.0, 3, 'Base in Puri/Konark and visit Astaranga/Ramachandi as half-day or sunset excursions.[web:268]', 'Stays in Puri or near Konark | A few small lodges/homestays near quieter beaches', 'Local seafood shacks and dhabas; better variety in Puri and Bhubaneswar.[web:268]', 8.0, 'Respect currents and avoid venturing too deep; beaches are less monitored than major resorts.', 'Mobile data works on main approach roads; can be weaker directly on remote stretches.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in Puri, Konark and village centres, not on beachline.', 'Odia | Hindi | Basic English in tourism.[web:268]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Fishing communities and temple-linked pilgrim circuits along Odisha coast.', 'Peak coastal energy around Rath Yatra in Puri; local village festivities at other times.', 'Ask before photographing fishermen or their catch; keep beaches clean, as waste management is limited.', 'Conches and souvenirs from Puri/Konark (avoid protected shells) | Local snacks from village stalls', 'Fresh fish curries from local shacks | Odia sweets from nearby towns', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 1800], "food_range": [200, 450], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [1500, 3550]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1800, 4000], "food_range": [350, 800], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [2950, 6600]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4000, 9000], "food_range": [700, 1500], "activities_range": [600, 1500], "local_transport_range": [500, 1000], "total_daily_range": [5800, 21000]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Astaranga & Ramachandi Beaches (Odisha Quiet Coast) in Odisha.', 'Highlighted in hidden-beach lists as calm, photogenic alternatives to busier Odisha shores.[web:265][web:268]', 'Growing attention in 2025 features on unexplored east-coast beaches, still with modest tourism build-out.[web:265][web:268]', 'Carry trash back to town bins and avoid disturbing turtle-nesting zones where relevant.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-85', 'Unakoti & North Tripura Heritage Belt', 'IN-TR', 'unakoti-north-tripura', 'Unakoti / North Tripura', 'North East India', 24.37, 92.05, 180, 6.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Agartala Airport (Maharaja Bir Bikram)", "distance_km": 165}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Kailashahar / Kumarghat (broad-gauge access)", "distance_km": 10}'::jsonb, 'Agartala', 165.0, 'Hilly roads from Agartala via Kailashahar/Kumarghat; improving connectivity as part of North East circuits.[web:269]', '{"Heritage","Rock_sculpture","Offbeat"}', '{"Unakoti rock-cut reliefs and sculptures in forested gorge","Local temples and village landscapes","Integration with wider Tripura heritage and nature circuits"}', '{"Heritage walks around sculptures","Short hikes and photography","Village visits as part of North East circuits"}', 'Ancient rock carvings of huge faces and reliefs carved into hill slopes, set amid lush vegetation and streams, still relatively little-known outside the region.[web:269]', 'Quieter viewpoints along the steps and pathways beyond main cluster | Nearby villages with traditional Tripuri life', 'November–March for comfortable temperatures and clearer skies.[web:269]', 'Heaviest monsoon months when paths can be slippery and access affected.', 'Winter weeks, especially when clubbed with wider North East tours.[web:269]', 'Hot pre-monsoon months and heavy-rain periods', '{"winter": "12-26\u00b0C", "summer": "26-36\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'High rainfall typical of North East hilly tracts with lush vegetation.[web:269]', '{"Heritage_enthusiasts","Offbeat_travellers","Photographers"}', '{"Heritage_enthusiasts": "Part of emerging heritage circuits in North East, featuring unique rock art not seen elsewhere in India.[web:269]", "Offbeat_travellers": "Remote feel and small-town hospitality away from major tourist hubs."}'::jsonb, 'Stairways and paths can be steep; basic footwear grip recommended; facilities on-site are simple.', 1.0, 1.0, 2, 'Include Unakoti as a day-trip or overnight halt in a broader Tripura–North East heritage and nature circuit.[web:269]', 'Basic hotels and guesthouses in nearby towns | Tourism department lodges (where available)', 'Local eateries with simple Bengali and Tripuri-style meals; limited variety.', 8.0, 'Generally safe and quiet; main risk is slips on wet steps in monsoon.', 'Mobile data in towns; may be weaker within gorge area.', 'BSNL | Jio | Airtel (coverage improving as per North East projects).[web:269]', 'ATMs in district towns; none at the heritage site itself.', 'Bengali | Kokborok (Tripuri) | Hindi and basic English in administration.[web:269]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Blend of tribal and Bengali cultures, with small-farm and forest-linked lifestyles.', 'Local fairs and religious gatherings; Unakoti Mela draws regional visitors.', 'Be respectful at active worship spots and avoid climbing on sculptures.', 'Simple local crafts and textiles in nearby markets', 'Simple fish and rice plates at local eateries | Regional snacks available in small shops', '{"accommodation_range": [700, 1500], "food_range": [200, 450], "activities_range": [200, 500], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [1400, 3150]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1500, 3200], "food_range": [350, 800], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [2650, 5800]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3200, 8000], "food_range": [700, 1500], "activities_range": [700, 1500], "local_transport_range": [500, 1000], "total_daily_range": [5100, 12000]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Unakoti & North Tripura Heritage Belt in Tripura.', 'Often labelled a ‘hidden Angkor-like’ site on a much smaller scale, appreciated by those seeking unusual heritage.[web:269]', 'Included in official tourism-circuit planning documents and funding announcements for North Eastern states.[web:269]', 'Avoid touching carvings, keep noise low and carry back all trash from forested valley.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-86', 'Mamallapuram (Mahabalipuram) & Coromandel Heritage Coast', 'IN-TN', 'chengalpattu', 'Chengalpattu', 'South India', 12.62, 80.19, 12, 9.0, 'Easy', '{"name": "Chennai International Airport", "distance_km": 55}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Chengalpattu / Chennai", "distance_km": 30}'::jsonb, 'Chennai', 50.0, 'Excellent roads along East Coast Road (ECR) and GST corridors; frequent buses and taxis from Chennai and Puducherry.[web:266][web:269]', '{"Heritage","Beach","Family","Weekend"}', '{"UNESCO-listed shore temple and rock-cut monuments","Five Rathas and Arjuna’s Penance bas-relief","ECR coastal drives with sea views","Nearby planned heritage and eco-park projects"}', '{"Heritage walks among rock-cut temples","Beach time on Coromandel coast","Short drives to DakshinaChitra and nearby attractions"}', 'Seaside temple town with some of India’s finest Pallava-era stone carving, easily combined with Chennai and Puducherry.[web:266][web:269]', 'Less-visited boulder clusters and shrines beyond main ticketed zone | Quieter stretches of ECR beaches on either side of town', 'November–February for pleasant coastal weather; evenings are comfortable much of the year.[web:266]', 'Peak monsoon/cyclone events and hottest April–May afternoons when humidity is high.', 'Winters, weekends and festival periods; also popular for school trips.[web:266]', 'Weekdays outside winter; some heat in shoulder seasons but manageable', '{"winter": "22-30\u00b0C", "summer": "28-38\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'North-east monsoon influenced; short but intense spells in Oct–Dec.[web:269]', '{"History_and_architecture_lovers","Families","Weekend_getaways_from_Chennai"}', '{"History_and_architecture_lovers": "Key site on India\u2019s heritage circuits with iconic rock-cut temples.[web:266][web:269]", "Weekend_getaways_from_Chennai": "Quick ECR access with beach resorts and heritage in one stop."}'::jsonb, 'Midday sun can be harsh among rock complexes; hats and hydration are essential.', 1.0, 2.0, 3, 'Day 1: Main monuments and shore temple; Day 2: Beachtime and side visits (DakshinaChitra, Crocodile Bank or ECR cafes).', 'Beach resorts | Budget guesthouses in town | Boutique hotels along ECR', 'Seafood and South Indian favourites, plus cafes catering to domestic and international tourists.', 9.0, 'Tourist-friendly; normal precautions; heed sea-safety flags.', 'Good 4G and broadband in town and resorts.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs available in town and along ECR.[web:269]', 'Tamil | English widely | Hindi understood in tourism.[web:266]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Temple town with artisans, fishermen and hospitality workers; strong Dravidian heritage.', 'Dance and cultural festivals sometimes held against heritage backdrops; nearby projects like Nandavanam Heritage Park are planned under tourism circuits.[web:269]', 'Dress modestly at temples; remove footwear where required.', 'Stone carvings and souvenirs | Shell craft and handicrafts', 'South Indian seafood curries | Filter coffee and tiffin items', '{"accommodation_range": [900, 2000], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [200, 500], "total_daily_range": [1550, 3600]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2000, 4500], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [3100, 7000]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4500, 16000], "food_range": [800, 2000], "activities_range": [700, 1800], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [6400, 20700]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Mamallapuram (Mahabalipuram) & Coromandel Heritage Coast in Tamil Nadu.', 'Regarded as a convenient and rewarding heritage stop with good combination of art, sea and resorts.', 'Featured in government tourism-circuit funding for heritage-park and eco-park enhancements.[web:269]', 'Avoid climbing on carvings or boulders where prohibited; keep beaches and monument areas clean.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-87', 'Hidden Goa Coves (Butterfly & Nearby Beaches)', 'IN-GA', 'south-goa', 'South Goa', 'West India', 15.01, 74.02, 0, 7.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Goa International (Dabolim) / MOPA (North Goa)", "distance_km": 65}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Canacona (for Palolem area)", "distance_km": 15}'::jsonb, 'Margao', 40.0, 'Accessible via internal roads and short hikes/boat rides from Palolem/Agonda region; suited to cabs and two-wheelers.[web:268]', '{"Beach","Offbeat","Short_break","Photography"}', '{"Butterfly Beach and other small coves near Canacona","Quieter sands than main stretches","Proximity to Palolem/Agonda for stay and food"}', '{"Boat trips or treks to hidden coves","Beach lounging and photography","Dolphin-spotting rides (regulated in some seasons)"}', 'Tucked-away coves that offer a more secluded feel than many of Goa’s crowded main beaches, especially on off-peak days.[web:268]', 'Early-morning visits to Butterfly and similar coves before boats arrive | Short hill trails connecting viewpoints above the sea', 'November–February for good sea conditions and pleasant weather.[web:268]', 'Monsoon when sea is rough and many boat services stop; access trails can be slippery.[web:268]', 'December–New Year weeks and long weekends; even then, early or weekday visits are calmer.[web:268]', 'Most non-holiday weekdays and shoulder months like November or February end', '{"winter": "22-32\u00b0C", "summer": "26-35\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-30\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Heavy Konkan monsoon shuts down most shacks and sea excursions.', '{"Couples","Small_groups","Quiet_beach_seekers"}', '{"Couples": "Secluded coves with scenic backdrops work well for relaxed, low-key days.[web:268]", "Quiet_beach_seekers": "Option to stay in livelier Palolem/Agonda while escaping to quieter sands by day.[web:268]"}'::jsonb, 'Carry drinking water and basic supplies; not all coves have shacks or lifeguards.', 1.0, 2.0, 4, 'Base in Palolem/Agonda for 2–4 nights, adding half-day trips to Butterfly and nearby coves on calm-sea days.[web:268]', 'Beach huts and guesthouses in Palolem/Agonda | Boutique stays in South Goa interior', 'Multi-cuisine shacks and cafes in main beaches; hidden coves may have nothing or one seasonal shack.[web:268]', 8.0, 'Watch tides and avoid isolated late-night stays on tiny coves; respect sea-safety advice.', 'Good 4G in nearby towns and main beaches; may be weak in certain headland spots.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in Canacona and other South Goa hubs.', 'Konkani | Hindi | English widely in tourism.[web:268]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Blend of fishing villages and tourism economy.', 'Goa-wide festival calendar; specific coves are more about natural ambience than events.', 'Respect local fishermen’s working hours and equipment stored on beaches.', 'Souvenirs and clothing from Palolem markets', 'Goan fish curry-rice | Seafood grills at nearby main beaches', '{"accommodation_range": [900, 2000], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [1650, 3800]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2000, 4500], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [3200, 7200]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4500, 14000], "food_range": [700, 1500], "activities_range": [700, 1800], "local_transport_range": [500, 1000], "total_daily_range": [6400, 18300]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Hidden Goa Coves (Butterfly & Nearby Beaches) in Goa.', 'Frequently appear in ‘hidden Goa’ lists, described as lovely when timed outside peak hours.[web:268]', 'Rising visibility in 2025 roundups of India’s hidden beaches, while access is still via simple trails/boats.[web:268]', 'Pack out all trash; these small coves have almost no waste handling capacity.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-88', 'Bangaram & Kadmat Islands (Lakshadweep Quiet Beaches)', 'IN-LA', 'union-territory', 'Union Territory', 'Island Territory', 10.86, 72.29, 0, 7.0, 'Difficult', '{"name": "Agatti Airport (Lakshadweep)", "distance_km": 15}'::jsonb, '{"name": "None (islands accessed by air/ship)", "distance_km": null}'::jsonb, 'Kochi (gateway by air/sea)', 440.0, 'Internal island roads only; external access via flights to Agatti and inter-island boats, subject to permits and schedules.[web:265]', '{"Island","Snorkelling","Offbeat_beach","Honeymoon"}', '{"Pristine white-sand beaches and lagoons","Snorkelling and kayaking in clear waters","Low tourist volumes due to entry restrictions"}', '{"Snorkelling and scuba (within regulations)","Kayaking and lagoon swims","Beach walks and stargazing"}', 'Highly restricted tropical islands where limited resorts and regulations keep beaches exceptionally quiet and ecologically intact.[web:265]', 'Less frequented parts of lagoon away from main jetties | Night skies with minimal light pollution', 'November–March for calmer seas and best visibility.[web:265]', 'South-west monsoon for rough seas and limited boat options; some services may halt.', 'December–February and national holiday blocks, though numbers are controlled.[web:265]', 'Monsoon and shoulder months when connectivity is weather-dependent', '{"winter": "24-30\u00b0C", "summer": "26-33\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-30\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Tropical maritime rainfall with strong winds during monsoon.', '{"Honeymooners","Snorkellers","Quiet_luxury_seekers"}', '{"Honeymooners": "Secluded beaches and limited visitor numbers create an exclusive feel.[web:265]", "Snorkellers": "Shallow lagoons and healthy reefs near shore in designated zones.[web:265]"}'::jsonb, 'Strict permit regime and limited transport; bookings must align with official guidelines and capacity constraints.', 3.0, 4.0, 7, 'Fly to Agatti from Kochi, connect by boat to chosen island, spend 3–5 nights enjoying lagoon activities and beach downtime.[web:265]', 'Government/authorised resorts | Limited private island stays', 'Buffet-style or set-menu dining in resorts with focus on seafood and Indian dishes.[web:265]', 9.0, 'Highly supervised; follow all lagoon-safety and reef-protection rules.', 'Limited; some resorts offer basic connectivity but expect partial digital detox.', 'BSNL primary; other networks limited or absent.', 'Very limited; payments generally arranged via packages and cards where available.', 'Malayalam | Hindi | Basic English in tourism.[web:265]', TRUE, 'Special entry permits required for Lakshadweep; only certain islands open to tourists and often via pre-booked packages.[web:265]', 'Islamic island communities with fishing and coconut-based livelihoods.', 'Local religious and community festivals; island stays focus on nature rather than events.', 'Dress modestly away from resort beach zones; respect local religious norms.', 'Very limited; some handicrafts and packaged coconut-based products', 'Fresh fish and coconut-based curries | Local snacks made from coconut and flour', '{"accommodation_range": [3500, 6000], "food_range": [800, 1500], "activities_range": [1500, 3000], "local_transport_range": [800, 1500], "total_daily_range": [6600, 12000]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [6000, 12000], "food_range": [1500, 2500], "activities_range": [2500, 4000], "local_transport_range": [1000, 2000], "total_daily_range": [11000, 20500]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [12000, 30000], "food_range": [2000, 3500], "activities_range": [3500, 6000], "local_transport_range": [1500, 3000], "total_daily_range": [19000, 42500]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Bangaram & Kadmat Islands (Lakshadweep Quiet Beaches) in Lakshadweep.', 'Described as among India’s most beautiful yet controlled island destinations; appreciated for quiet and clarity of water.[web:265]', 'Featured in 2026 travel-trend lists as offbeat but restricted, with emphasis on ecological balance.[web:265][web:255]', 'Use reef-safe sunscreen, avoid touching corals and abide by all restrictions on fishing and shell collection.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-89', 'Malanad–Malabar Backwater & Rural Belt', 'IN-KE', 'multiple-kasargod', 'Multiple (Kasargod, Kannur, Malnad coastal districts)', 'South India', 12.35, 75.15, 10, 6.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Mangaluru / Kannur International Airport", "distance_km": 80}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Various coastal stations (e.g., Kasargod, Kannur)", "distance_km": 10}'::jsonb, 'Mangaluru / Kozhikode', 100.0, 'Access via NH66 and interior roads; promoted as part of Malanad Malabar Cruise and rural circuits tying rivers, backwaters and villages.[web:266]', '{"Backwaters","Rural","Slow_travel","Culture"}', '{"Rivers, backwaters and village landscapes","Slow boat cruises as part of Malanad Malabar Cruise Tourism","Local temples, theyyams (seasonal) and coastal life"}', '{"Backwater and river cruising","Village walks and homestays","Temple visits and cultural interactions"}', 'Less-commercialised backwater and rural zones compared to central Kerala, with combined Karnataka–Kerala culture.[web:266]', 'Small village jetties and local ferries | Homestays participating in rural circuit programmes', 'November–March for comfortable temperatures and navigable water levels.[web:266]', 'Peak monsoon floods and very humid shoulder weeks; boat schedules can change.', 'Winter months when circuits and cruises see more bookings.[web:266]', 'Rains and off-peak months; good for very quiet, local-focused stays', '{"winter": "22-32\u00b0C", "summer": "26-35\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-30\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Heavy South West monsoon; region turns intensely green.', '{"Slow_travellers","Culture_seekers","Families"}', '{"Slow_travellers": "Rural circuit explicitly built around unhurried village and waterway experiences.[web:266]", "Culture_seekers": "Chance to observe temple arts like theyyam and local rituals at close quarters."}'::jsonb, 'Circuit is still developing; some logistics like cruise departures and homestay quality vary.', 2.0, 3.0, 6, 'Combine 2–4 days of Malanad–Malabar cruising and village homestays with nearby beaches or hill stations.[web:266]', 'Homestays | Small backwater resorts | Basic lodges in small towns', 'Home-style Malabar and coastal Karnataka cuisine with rice, fish and coconut dominating.', 9.0, 'Safe rural belt; main concerns are water safety and monsoon conditions.', '4G in most villages near main roads; weaker in interior waterways.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in nearby towns; cash still useful in small villages.', 'Malayalam | Kannada | Tulu | Hindi/English to varying degrees.[web:266]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Blend of Kerala and coastal Karnataka traditions in food, dress and temple architecture.', 'Theyyam season in North Kerala and multiple temple festivals; rural circuit itineraries often overlap festival times.[web:266]', 'Observe temple dress codes and separate areas for non-Hindus where applicable.', 'Local spices and snacks | Small handicrafts and coir products', 'Malabar fish curry | Appam with stew | Local coastal snacks like pathiri variants', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 2000], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [1550, 3800]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2000, 4500], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [3200, 7200]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4500, 12000], "food_range": [700, 1500], "activities_range": [700, 1800], "local_transport_range": [500, 1000], "total_daily_range": [6400, 16300]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Malanad–Malabar Backwater & Rural Belt in Kerala & Karnataka (bordering regions).', 'Still niche but appreciated by travellers looking beyond mainstream Kerala backwaters.', 'Identified as part of Rural Circuit (Malanad Malabar Cruise Tourism) in national tourism-circuit plans.[web:266]', 'Opt for eco-certified cruises and homestays; keep waterways free of litter and respect village privacy.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-90', 'Krishna Heritage Circuit (Mathura–Vrindavan–Dwarka Focus)', 'IN-UT', 'multiple', 'Multiple', 'Multi-state', 27.5, 77.67, 170, 9.0, 'Easy', '{"name": "Multiple gateways (Delhi for Mathura\u2013Vrindavan, Jamnagar/Rajkot for Dwarka)", "distance_km": 60}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Mathura Junction / Vrindavan branch / Dwarka", "distance_km": 2}'::jsonb, 'Delhi / Ahmedabad (depending segment)', 150.0, 'Part of nationally promoted Krishna Circuit covering key sites in UP, Gujarat, Rajasthan, Haryana and Odisha; main nodes have strong highway and rail links.[web:266]', '{"Spiritual","Heritage","Pilgrimage","Family"}', '{"Mathura and Vrindavan temples associated with Krishna’s early life","Dwarkadhish Temple at Dwarka in Gujarat","Additional nodes in Rajasthan, Haryana and Odisha under the Krishna Circuit"}', '{"Temple darshans and aartis","Heritage walks in old temple towns","Participation in festivals and kirtans"}', 'Multi-state circuit centred on the life and legends of Krishna, linking riverfront ghats, historic temples and coastal shrines.[web:266]', 'Smaller ashrams and older shrines away from main temple queues | Quieter ghats visited early morning or late evening', 'October–March for manageable temperatures on north and west Indian plains.[web:266]', 'Hottest summer months for long queues and heat stress; monsoon for some travel disruptions.', 'Janmashtami and major festival periods; long weekends and school vacations.', 'Non-festival weekdays outside winter', '{"winter": "8-24\u00b0C (north) / 14-28\u00b0C (coastal)", "summer": "26-42\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Typical monsoon on plains and Saurashtra coast; some temples see crowds during Shravan/monsoon festivals.', '{"Devotees","Culture_seekers","Families"}', '{"Devotees": "Designated national Krishna Circuit connects multiple major temples with improved infrastructure.[web:266]", "Culture_seekers": "Chance to experience bhajans, kirtans and temple-town street life across regions."}'::jsonb, 'Crowding around festival dates; accommodation in temple towns should be booked early during Janmashtami or big yatras.', 2.0, 4.0, 10, 'Short trips might focus on Mathura–Vrindavan only; longer yatras add Dwarka and intermediate nodes across states.[web:266]', 'Dharamshalas and ashrams | Budget and mid-range hotels | Some higher-end hotels in larger nodes', 'Predominantly vegetarian with many satvik and temple-linked eateries.', 8.0, 'Temple-town pickpocketing possible in crowds; take usual precautions and keep hydrated.', 'Good 4G in main towns; some ashrams emphasize low-tech stays.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'Widely available in main circuit towns.[web:266]', 'Hindi | Gujarati (in Gujarat nodes) | English in tourism and larger temples.[web:266]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Strong Vaishnav devotional traditions with daily rituals, bhajans and prasad offerings.', 'Janmashtami, Holi in Braj region, Kartik and other key Vaishnav festivals draw large crowds.[web:266]', 'Dress modestly, especially in temple interiors; remove footwear and follow queue systems.', 'Religious books, idols and accessories | Local sweets like peda (Mathura) and prasad items', 'Mathura peda and lassi | Simple satvik thalis | Local farsan and snacks in Gujarat nodes', '{"accommodation_range": [700, 1800], "food_range": [200, 450], "activities_range": [100, 400], "local_transport_range": [200, 500], "total_daily_range": [1200, 3150]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1800, 4000], "food_range": [300, 700], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [2600, 6000]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4000, 12000], "food_range": [600, 1200], "activities_range": [400, 1000], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [5400, 15100]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Krishna Heritage Circuit (Mathura–Vrindavan–Dwarka Focus) in Uttar Pradesh, Gujarat, others.', 'Considered spiritually fulfilling and logistically straightforward thanks to strong connectivity between main nodes.', 'Officially listed Krishna Circuit under national tourism with funding for facility upgrades across multiple states.[web:266]', 'Use refillable bottles, avoid plastic offerings where alternatives exist and respect queue etiquette to keep flows smooth.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-91', 'Rishikesh & Haridwar (Himalayan Yoga Route)', 'IN-UT', 'dehradun-haridwar', 'Dehradun / Haridwar', 'North India', 30.12, 78.29, 372, 10.0, 'Easy', '{"name": "Dehradun (Jolly Grant) Airport", "distance_km": 20}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Haridwar Junction / Rishikesh", "distance_km": 0}'::jsonb, 'Dehradun', 45.0, 'Excellent highway and bus connectivity from Delhi, Dehradun and other north Indian cities.[web:273][web:274][web:277]', '{"Spiritual","Yoga","Ganga_ghats","Adventure"}', '{"Ganga Aarti at Haridwar and Rishikesh ghats","Ashrams and yoga/meditation centres","Suspension bridges like Lakshman Jhula (and new bridge)","Rafting and short hikes in surrounding hills"}', '{"Yoga classes and retreats","Evening Ganga Aarti","White-water rafting (seasonal)","Temple and ashram visits"}', 'Gateway to the Himalayas where Ganga emerges from the hills, combining yoga, spiritual stays and soft adventure.[web:273][web:274][web:277]', 'Small ashrams upriver from main town ghats | Quiet morning walks on less-crowded river stretches', 'September–April for comfortable weather and active yoga/retreat calendar.[web:273][web:274]', 'Peak monsoon for high river levels and landslides; high summer afternoons can be hot in Haridwar.[web:274]', 'Festivals, long weekends and winter months; Char Dham season brings high pilgrim flows through Haridwar–Rishikesh.[web:273][web:277]', 'Monsoon and very hot weeks before rains, except for serious sadhaks who stay year-round', '{"winter": "6-22\u00b0C", "summer": "24-38\u00b0C", "monsoon": "22-30\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'North Indian monsoon with occasional intense spells that raise Ganga levels.[web:274]', '{"Yoga_seekers","First_time_spiritual_travellers","Families"}', '{"Yoga_seekers": "Global reputation as \u2018yoga capital\u2019, with teacher-training and shorter retreats.[web:273][web:274]", "First_time_spiritual_travellers": "Easy logistics and wide range of ashrams and hotels at different budgets.[web:273]"}'::jsonb, 'Alcohol and non-vegetarian food are restricted in many parts of Rishikesh; respect river safety advisories during rafting and high flow.', 2.0, 3.0, 7, 'Combine Haridwar evening Aarti with 2–5 days in Rishikesh focusing on yoga, river walks and short hill excursions.[web:273][web:274]', 'Ashrams and dharamshalas | Budget guesthouses | Boutique Ganga-facing resorts', 'Predominantly vegetarian with many cafes serving Indian and continental health-focused dishes.[web:273]', 9.0, 'Very popular with solo and foreign travellers; main risks are river currents and occasional crowd surges at ghats.', 'Strong 4G and Wi‑Fi in most ashrams, cafes and hotels.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'Ample ATMs in both towns.', 'Hindi | Garhwali | English widely in tourism.[web:273]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Deeply religious Ganga-town culture with daily rituals, kirtans and satsangs.', 'Kumbh (periodic in Haridwar), Kanwar Yatra, Ganga Dussehra and numerous ashram events.[web:277]', 'Dress modestly at ghats and temples; avoid photography during worship where restricted.', 'Rudraksha beads and spiritual books | Ayurvedic products and yoga gear', 'Simple ashram thalis | Street-side chole–bhature and lassi in Haridwar', '{"accommodation_range": [600, 1600], "food_range": [150, 350], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [150, 400], "total_daily_range": [1100, 2950]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1600, 3500], "food_range": [300, 700], "activities_range": [400, 1000], "local_transport_range": [200, 500], "total_daily_range": [2500, 5700]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3500, 15000], "food_range": [600, 1500], "activities_range": [700, 2000], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [5100, 19200]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Rishikesh & Haridwar (Himalayan Yoga Route) in Uttarakhand.', 'Frequently rated among India’s top spiritual journeys, combining accessibility with a strong yoga and Ganga focus.[web:273][web:274]', 'Featured in multiple ‘spiritual journeys’ and ‘Himalayan yoga route’ write‑ups for 2025.[web:274][web:277]', 'Avoid plastic near the river, participate in ghat clean‑ups where offered and use biodegradable offerings.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-92', 'Varanasi Ganga Ghats Pilgrimage', 'IN-UP', 'varanasi', 'Varanasi', 'North India', 25.31, 83.01, 80, 10.0, 'Easy', '{"name": "Varanasi (Lal Bahadur Shastri) Airport", "distance_km": 22}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Varanasi Junction / Banaras", "distance_km": 2}'::jsonb, 'Prayagraj', 120.0, 'Connected to major north Indian cities by highways and frequent trains; city traffic is dense in old quarters.[web:274][web:276][web:277]', '{"Spiritual","Heritage","Ganga_ghats"}', '{"Ganga ghats including Dashashwamedh and Assi","Kashi Vishwanath Temple corridor","Morning and evening Ganga Aarti","Boat rides on the river"}', '{"Sunrise and sunset boat rides","Walking tours of lanes and ghats","Temple darshans and ritual observance"}', 'One of the world’s oldest living cities, with continuous ritual life along the Ganga and dense historic lanes.[web:274][web:276][web:277]', 'Less-crowded southern ghats near Assi in early morning | Small akharas and temples tucked inside alleys', 'October–March for more comfortable temperatures and clear river mornings.[web:274][web:276]', 'Peak summer heat and humidity; some monsoon weeks with very high river levels.', 'Winter months, festivals like Dev Deepawali and Kartik Purnima; also popular during key Hindu festivals.[web:274][web:277]', 'Mid-summer and parts of monsoon (excluding festival dates)', '{"winter": "8-24\u00b0C", "summer": "26-42\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Typical Ganga plain monsoon; high water can submerge lower ghat steps.', '{"Spiritual_travellers","Photographers","Culture_seekers"}', '{"Spiritual_travellers": "Ghats and temples form a focused \u2018Varanasi Ganga Ghats Pilgrimage\u2019 route highlighted in modern spiritual itineraries.[web:274][web:277]", "Photographers": "Atmospheric light, boats and rituals create powerful visual scenes."}'::jsonb, 'Crowded and intense; stay aware of belongings in narrow lanes and respect people’s privacy during funerary rituals.', 2.0, 3.0, 5, 'Mix 2–3 ghats per day with one sunrise and one evening Aarti boat, plus time in Kashi Vishwanath corridor and old city walks.[web:274]', 'Ghat-facing guesthouses | Budget hotels | Heritage and boutique stays', 'Mostly vegetarian, with street food staples like kachori–sabzi, chaat and sweets, plus cafes in touristy pockets.[web:274]', 8.0, 'Chaotic but generally safe; main risks are crowds, traffic and occasional scams.', 'Good 4G in most parts of the city; some ghats have patchier coverage.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'Numerous ATMs across city.', 'Hindi | Bhojpuri | English widely used with tourists.[web:274]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Strongly devotional Hindu culture with continuous aartis, yagya and Sanskrit chanting traditions.', 'Dev Deepawali, Kartik month rituals, Holi (nearby), and countless local temple festivals.[web:274][web:277]', 'Dress modestly; remove footwear at temples; avoid photography at cremation ghats unless explicitly allowed.', 'Rudraksha, religious books and brassware | Silk sarees from local weavers', 'Banarasi paan | Kachori–sabzi and jalebi breakfast | Lassi from traditional shops', '{"accommodation_range": [700, 1800], "food_range": [200, 450], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [200, 500], "total_daily_range": [1300, 3350]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1800, 4000], "food_range": [300, 700], "activities_range": [300, 800], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [2700, 6200]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4000, 18000], "food_range": [600, 1200], "activities_range": [500, 1200], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [5500, 21300]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Varanasi Ganga Ghats Pilgrimage in Uttar Pradesh.', 'Described as intense, moving and unforgettable; often included in ‘transformative routes’ lists for spiritual India.[web:274][web:277]', 'New Kashi Vishwanath corridor infrastructure and riverfront improvements have changed visitor flows in recent years.[web:272][web:277]', 'Use eco-friendly offerings, avoid throwing plastic into the river and support ghats that host clean‑up efforts.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
