eb:274]', 'Peak summer heat; some monsoon periods for humidity and waterlogging.', 'Winter months, especially around major Buddhist festivals and teaching events.[web:274]', 'Hot months with fewer foreign groups; useful for very quiet retreats', '{"winter": "8-24\u00b0C", "summer": "28-42\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Ganga plain monsoon with occasional heavy spells.[web:274]', '{"Meditation_practitioners","Buddhist_pilgrims","Culture_seekers"}', '{"Meditation_practitioners": "Highlighted as a core stop on the \u2018Bodh Gaya Buddhist Circuit\u2019 route in spiritual travel features.[web:274]", "Buddhist_pilgrims": "Global Buddhist community convergence with teachings, retreats and ceremonies."}'::jsonb, 'Respect temple rules regarding silence, dress and photography; security can be tight during peak events.', 2.0, 3.0, 5, 'Spend 2–3 days based in Bodh Gaya combining temple time, monastery visits and short trips to nearby associated sites.[web:274]', 'Guesthouses | Pilgrim lodges | Mid-range hotels', 'Simple vegetarian and multi‑cuisine cafes serving travellers and monastic communities.[web:274]', 8.0, 'Pilgrimage town; normal precautions; avoid very late‑night solitary walks away from main zones.', '4G in town; Wi‑Fi in most guesthouses and cafes.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in town and nearby city of Gaya.', 'Hindi | Magahi/Bhojpuri | English commonly used with pilgrims.[web:274]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Mix of local Bihari communities with international Buddhist presence.', 'Buddha Purnima and periodic large‑scale teachings by senior monks and teachers.[web:274]', 'Dress modestly and move clockwise (pradakshina) around sacred structures as per traditions.', 'Buddhist statues and ritual items | Books and CDs on meditation and teachings', 'Simple thalis at pilgrim restaurants | Tea and snacks at monastery canteens', '{"accommodation_range": [700, 1800], "food_range": [200, 450], "activities_range": [200, 500], "local_transport_range": [200, 500], "total_daily_range": [1300, 3250]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1800, 3800], "food_range": [300, 700], "activities_range": [300, 800], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [2700, 6000]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3800, 12000], "food_range": [600, 1200], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [5200, 15300]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Bodh Gaya Buddhist Circuit Hub in Bihar.', 'Frequently described as calm and deeply contemplative, particularly beyond peak hours in temple complex.[web:274]', 'Highlighted among key UNESCO‑linked spiritual circuits and improved under national tourism schemes.[web:272][web:276]', 'Help keep temple grounds quiet and clean; avoid overuse of plastic near sacred areas.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-94', 'Rameswaram & Pamban Coast (Sacred Water Walk)', 'IN-TN', 'ramanathapuram', 'Ramanathapuram', 'South India', 9.29, 79.31, 10, 8.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Madurai Airport", "distance_km": 175}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Rameswaram", "distance_km": 1}'::jsonb, 'Madurai', 170.0, 'Linked to mainland via iconic Pamban Bridge; buses and cars connect from Madurai and other Tamil Nadu cities.[web:274][web:276]', '{"Spiritual","Coastal","Pilgrimage"}', '{"Ramanathaswamy Temple and long pillared corridors","Sacred ‘teerthams’ (water bodies) and sea dips","Pamban Bridge views and coastal scenery"}', '{"Temple darshans and ritual baths at designated wells/ghats","Walks along sea and bridge viewpoints","Short drives to Dhanushkodi ruins and beaches"}', 'A coastal pilgrimage combining legendary Ramayana associations with a ritual walk through multiple sacred water points.[web:274]', 'Early‑morning temple visits before crowds build | Quiet stretches of coast near Dhanushkodi on non‑holiday weekdays', 'October–March for relatively milder heat and calmer seas.[web:274]', 'Peak summer and days with active cyclonic systems in Bay of Bengal.', 'Festival periods, school vacations and long weekends; temple lines can be long.[web:274]', 'Non‑festival weekdays outside winter', '{"winter": "22-30\u00b0C", "summer": "28-36\u00b0C", "monsoon": "26-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Influenced by both south‑west and north‑east monsoon, with heaviest spells in Oct–Dec.[web:274]', '{"Devotees","Culture_plus_sea_travellers","Families"}', '{"Devotees": "Listed in spiritual\u2011journey guides as \u2018Rameswaram Sacred Water Walk\u2019 for its many teerthams.[web:274]", "Culture_plus_sea_travellers": "Temple plus coastal landscapes and Pamban views make for a rounded trip."}'::jsonb, 'Strict dress norms for certain temple areas; check timings and rules for water rituals; sea can have strong currents.', 1.0, 2.0, 3, 'One full day for main temple and teerthams; additional day for Dhanushkodi and relaxed coast drives.[web:274]', 'Pilgrim lodges | Budget and mid‑range hotels | A few seaside resorts', 'Vegetarian and coastal South Indian cuisine dominated by tiffin items and thalis.', 9.0, 'Pilgrim town; common‑sense precautions; follow official warnings about sea entry.', 'Functional 4G in town; patchy in some outlying coastal stretches.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in town and on approach roads.', 'Tamil | Hindi (to some extent) | English in tourism.[web:274]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Devotional Shaivite town with strong temple economy and seafaring links.', 'Shivratri and other major Hindu festival days see big inflows.[web:274]', 'Maintain decorum during rituals; follow temple queues and instructions from priests.', 'Religious souvenirs and shells (ensure not from protected species) | Local snacks and sweets', 'South Indian filter coffee | Temple‑town vegetarian meals', '{"accommodation_range": [700, 1600], "food_range": [200, 450], "activities_range": [100, 400], "local_transport_range": [200, 400], "total_daily_range": [1200, 2850]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1600, 3500], "food_range": [300, 700], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [300, 600], "total_daily_range": [2400, 5450]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3500, 10000], "food_range": [600, 1200], "activities_range": [400, 800], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [4800, 12700]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Rameswaram & Pamban Coast (Sacred Water Walk) in Tamil Nadu.', 'Described as spiritually intense and visually striking due to long corridors and the surrounding sea.[web:274]', 'Featured as ‘Rameswaram Sacred Water Walk’ in recent spiritual‑route articles, highlighting teertham sequences.[web:274]', 'Avoid soap/shampoo in sea or teerthams; use eco‑friendly offerings and minimise plastic at ghats.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
