es and river‑side ghats in Hampi | Smaller structures in Aihole with early experimentation', 'October–March for bearable daytime heat and clearer skies.[web:276][web:279]', 'Peak summer; some monsoon weeks when paths become slick among boulders.', 'Winter holidays and long weekends; also around major local festivals.[web:276]', 'Shoulder months and hotter weeks (for those tolerant of heat)', '{"winter": "16-30\u00b0C", "summer": "26-40\u00b0C", "monsoon": "22-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Semi‑arid with moderate monsoon; boulders and ruins dry quickly after showers.[web:276]', '{"History_buffs","Architecture_lovers","Backpackers"}', '{"History_buffs": "Featured in UNESCO circuits as must\u2011visit for Vijayanagara and Chalukyan architecture.[web:276][web:279]", "Architecture_lovers": "Mix of Dravidian and Nagara styles, cave temples and monumental complexes."}'::jsonb, 'Large area and strong sun; plan early‑morning and late‑afternoon sightseeing and carry enough water.', 2.0, 3.0, 5, 'Spend 2–3 days around Hampi core ruins, then 1–2 days for Pattadakal–Badami–Aihole day trips or overnights.[web:276][web:279]', 'Guesthouses in Hampi/Hosapete | Mid‑range hotels | A few upscale resorts', 'Simple South Indian, North Indian and traveller‑oriented cafes near main bazaar zones.[web:279]', 9.0, 'Generally safe; be cautious on boulder edges and deserted ruins after dark.', '4G in Hosapete and most village cores; may weaken inside deeper ruin clusters.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in Hosapete and main villages.', 'Kannada | Hindi | English used widely in tourism.[web:279]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Rural Karnataka communities interwoven with heritage tourism economy.', 'Hampi Utsav and other cultural events highlight music and dance against monument backdrops.[web:276]', 'Avoid climbing on fragile structures; follow ASI guidelines at sites.', 'Local handicrafts and small stone carvings | Simple souvenirs and textiles', 'South Indian tiffin at local eateries | Special vegetarian thalis', '{"accommodation_range": [800, 2000], "food_range": [250, 500], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [1550, 3800]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [2000, 4500], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [400, 900], "local_transport_range": [400, 900], "total_daily_range": [3200, 7200]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [4500, 15000], "food_range": [700, 1500], "activities_range": [700, 1800], "local_transport_range": [500, 1000], "total_daily_range": [6400, 19300]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Hampi & Pattadakal (UNESCO Vijayanagara–Chalukya Circuit) in Karnataka.', 'Rated as one of India’s most rewarding heritage landscapes, with many visitors recommending at least 3 days.[web:276][web:279]', 'Featured among ‘UNESCO World Heritage circuits’ and in South India UNESCO tours.[web:276][web:279]', 'Stick to marked paths, avoid graffiti and support local guides trained in heritage interpretation.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-96', 'Gulmarg (Kashmir Ski & Snow Destination)', 'IN-JA', 'baramulla', 'Baramulla', 'North India', 34.05, 74.38, 2650, 9.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Srinagar Airport", "distance_km": 50}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Srinagar/Udhampur (via road)", "distance_km": 50}'::jsonb, 'Srinagar', 50.0, 'Hill road from Srinagar to Gulmarg; winter snow can impact driving time but route is popular and well‑used.[web:275][web:278]', '{"Skiing","Snow_destination","Mountain"}', '{"Gulmarg Gondola (one of highest cable cars)","Deep‑snow ski slopes and powder runs","Meadows and pine forests turning into ski terrain in winter"}', '{"Skiing and snowboarding (varied difficulty)","Snow play and sledging","Gondola rides for vistas and high‑altitude access"}', 'Global‑level ski terrain with high‑altitude powder slopes and a famous gondola, set within classic Kashmir scenery.[web:275][web:278]', 'Off‑piste runs for advanced skiers with guides | Quieter snow meadows away from main crowd belts', 'December–March for snow sports, with peak conditions often Jan–Feb.[web:275][web:278]', 'Shoulder weeks with slushy snow; heavy storm days when lifts may be closed.', 'Winter school holidays and long weekends; also busy in summer for meadows and views.[web:275]', 'Late spring and autumn shoulder periods with fewer visitors', '{"winter": "-8-6\u00b0C", "summer": "10-22\u00b0C", "monsoon": "12-20\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Snowfall dominates winter; shoulder months see rain/snow mix.', '{"Skiers_and_snowboarders","Snow_lovers","Adventure_travellers"}', '{"Skiers_and_snowboarders": "Described as \u2018Himalayan ski paradise\u2019 with terrain for beginners to professionals.[web:275][web:278]", "Adventure_travellers": "Heli\u2011skiing and off\u2011piste options suit experienced riders.[web:278]"}'::jsonb, 'Avalanche and weather risks at higher slopes; always ski with certified guides and follow official advisories.[web:278]', 2.0, 3.0, 7, 'Base in Gulmarg for 3–5 days with mix of lessons, free skiing and gondola‑top sessions, plus Srinagar side‑trip before/after.[web:278]', 'Heritage hotels | Modern ski resorts | Budget lodges', 'Kashmiri and North Indian dishes with hearty winter meals in hotels and dhabas.[web:275]', 7.0, 'Terrain and snowpack present real risks; choose reputable operators for skiing and gondola‑top activities.[web:278]', 'Variable; main hotels usually offer Wi‑Fi; mobile data quality depends on current J&K restrictions and networks.', 'Jio | Airtel and others subject to regional policy at the time.[web:278]', 'Limited ATMs in/around Gulmarg; carry some cash from Srinagar.', 'Kashmiri | Urdu | Hindi | English in tourism.[web:275]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Mountain communities with tourism and pastoral livelihoods; winter economy strongly ski‑oriented.', 'Winter sports events and ski competitions occasionally organised.', 'Negotiation for sleds/ponies is common; agree prices clearly beforehand.', 'Woollens and pashmina (better verified in Srinagar) | Small souvenirs in local shops', 'Kashmiri wazwan dishes (mostly in Srinagar) | Noon chai and kahwa', '{"accommodation_range": [1500, 3000], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [1200, 2500], "local_transport_range": [500, 1200], "total_daily_range": [3600, 7600]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3000, 7000], "food_range": [700, 1500], "activities_range": [2000, 3500], "local_transport_range": [700, 1500], "total_daily_range": [6400, 13500]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [7000, 22000], "food_range": [1200, 2500], "activities_range": [3000, 6000], "local_transport_range": [1000, 2000], "total_daily_range": [12200, 32700]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Gulmarg (Kashmir Ski & Snow Destination) in Jammu and Kashmir.', 'Frequently cited as India’s premier adventure ski destination with stunning views and serious powder.[web:275][web:278]', 'Highlighted in 2025–26 lists of top snow destinations and ski‑comparisons with Auli.[web:275][web:278]', 'Respect off‑piste guidelines; avoid littering slopes and support operators who follow mountain‑safety norms.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
