days.', 'Full‑moon nights and Karthigai Deepam festival when massive crowds arrive.[web:274]', 'Non‑festival weekdays and off‑moon days for quieter stays', '{"winter": "20-30\u00b0C", "summer": "28-40\u00b0C", "monsoon": "24-32\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Receives north‑east monsoon rains in Oct–Dec.', '{"Meditation_seekers","Spiritual_solo_travellers","Ashram_visitors"}', '{"Meditation_seekers": "Recommended as \u2018Inner Fire Journey\u2019 in spiritual\u2011routes lists, focused on introspection and self\u2011enquiry.[web:274]", "Ashram_visitors": "Multiple ashrams and satsang centres near Arunachala."}'::jsonb, 'Crowds and traffic around full‑moon girivalam; book stays early for major festival dates.', 2.0, 3.0, 7, 'Split time between temple visits, one full girivalam and quiet days at ashram or retreat centres.[web:274]', 'Ashram guest rooms | Budget lodges | Simple hotels and a few boutique stays', 'Mostly vegetarian tiffin and thalis; ashram food is simple and sattvic.', 8.0, 'Town is busy but manageable; avoid walking isolated stretches late at night without company.', '4G in town; some ashrams intentionally keep Wi‑Fi limited.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'ATMs in town centre.', 'Tamil | Hindi to some extent | English at ashrams.[web:274]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Strong Shaivite devotional culture with continuous worship and pilgrim movement.', 'Karthigai Deepam, full‑moon girivalam days and numerous temple festivals.[web:274]', 'Dress modestly; many people walk girivalam barefoot as a vow.', 'Religious books and photos | Incense and small souvenirs', 'Simple South Indian meals | Filter coffee in local tiffin shops', '{"accommodation_range": [600, 1500], "food_range": [150, 400], "activities_range": [100, 300], "local_transport_range": [150, 400], "total_daily_range": [1000, 2600]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1500, 3200], "food_range": [250, 600], "activities_range": [150, 400], "local_transport_range": [200, 500], "total_daily_range": [2100, 4700]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3200, 9000], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [300, 700], "total_daily_range": [4100, 11200]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Tiruvannamalai & Arunachala (Inner Fire Journey) in Tamil Nadu.', 'Regarded as intense but inward‑focused pilgrimage town; many visitors return annually for spiritual practice.[web:274]', 'Highlighted as ‘Tiruvannamalai Inner Fire Journey’ in long‑form spiritual route guides.[web:274]', 'Keep the girivalam path clean, avoid plastic offerings and respect forested flanks of Arunachala.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-99', 'Amarkantak Nature–Spiritual Loop', 'IN-MA', 'anuppur-region', 'Anuppur region', 'Central India', 22.67, 81.75, 1065, 6.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Jabalpur / Raipur (farther)", "distance_km": 230}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Pendra Road / Anuppur", "distance_km": 40}'::jsonb, 'Jabalpur / Bilaspur', 230.0, 'Hilly forest roads connect from Madhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh; part of emerging nature‑spiritual itineraries.[web:274]', '{"Spiritual","Nature","Offbeat"}', '{"Source region of Narmada and Son rivers","Temples and ashrams amidst forests","Nearby waterfalls and viewpoints"}', '{"Temple and river‑source visits","Short hikes to falls and forest viewpoints","Meditation and ashram stays"}', 'Jungle‑edge plateau with river origins, mixing quiet nature with low‑key spiritual sites.[web:274]', 'Less‑visited streams and smaller shrines in forested areas | Off‑peak weekday walks along river‑source paths', 'October–March for cool, dry weather and walkable trails.[web:274]', 'Heavy monsoon for leechy, slippery trails; very hot pre‑monsoon months.', 'Winter vacation weeks and certain festival dates.[web:274]', 'Monsoon and hot months; suited only to those prepared for basic conditions', '{"winter": "10-24\u00b0C", "summer": "24-36\u00b0C", "monsoon": "20-28\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Forest plateau monsoon; streams and waterfalls swell in rains.[web:274]', '{"Nature_spiritual_seekers","Offbeat_travellers","Small_groups"}', '{"Nature_spiritual_seekers": "Highlighted as \u2018Amarkantak Nature\u2013Spiritual Loop\u2019 blending river origins and simple ashrams.[web:274]", "Offbeat_travellers": "Low footfall and basic facilities keep it relatively uncommercial."}'::jsonb, 'Facilities and healthcare are basic; good for those comfortable with small‑town infrastructure.', 2.0, 2.0, 4, 'Spend 2–3 nights visiting river sources, nearby falls and ashrams, combining with wider MP/Chhattisgarh trips.[web:274]', 'Simple lodges | Dharamshalas and ashram stays', 'Basic vegetarian meals; limited restaurant variety.', 8.0, 'Quiet and generally safe; exercise caution on forest trails and near waterfall edges.', 'Limited; some 4G near town centre, weaker deeper into forest.', 'Jio | Airtel | BSNL (patchy in some areas).[web:274]', 'ATMs in nearby small towns; carry cash for local spending.', 'Hindi | Local dialects | Very limited English.[web:274]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Central Indian hill communities with strong river‑reverence traditions.', 'Local river festivals and religious gatherings at origin points.[web:274]', 'Maintain silence and cleanliness at river‑source spots regarded as highly sacred.', 'Small religious items and local snacks', 'Simple thalis at local dhabas', '{"accommodation_range": [600, 1500], "food_range": [150, 400], "activities_range": [100, 300], "local_transport_range": [200, 500], "total_daily_range": [1050, 2700]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1500, 3200], "food_range": [250, 600], "activities_range": [150, 400], "local_transport_range": [300, 600], "total_daily_range": [2200, 4800]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3200, 8000], "food_range": [400, 900], "activities_range": [200, 600], "local_transport_range": [400, 800], "total_daily_range": [4200, 10300]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Amarkantak Nature–Spiritual Loop in Madhya Pradesh / Chhattisgarh border.', 'Not as famous as big pilgrim towns but appreciated by those seeking a green, uncrowded spiritual escape.[web:274]', 'Appears in new ‘spiritual journeys’ lists as a nature‑linked alternative to urban centres.[web:274]', 'Carry trash out of forests, avoid loud music and respect wildlife presence on trails.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO destinations (id, destination_name, state_id, city_id, district, region, latitude, longitude, altitude_m, popularity_score, accessibility, nearest_airport, nearest_railway, nearest_major_city, nearest_major_city_distance_km, road_connectivity, trip_types, primary_attractions, activities_available, unique_experiences, hidden_gems, best_seasons, avoid_seasons, peak_season, off_season, average_temperature, rainfall_pattern, ideal_for, ideal_for_why, special_considerations, minimum_days, ideal_days, maximum_days, suggested_itinerary, accommodation_types, food_scene, safety_rating, safety_notes, internet_connectivity, mobile_network, atm_availability, language_spoken, permits_required, permits_details, local_culture, festivals_events, local_customs, shopping_highlights, local_cuisine_must_try, budget_range_json, mid_range_json, luxury_range_json, description, user_reviews_summary, recent_developments, sustainability_notes) VALUES ('dest-100', 'Haridwar–Rishikesh–Char Dham Spiritual Trail (Meta‑Circuit Node)', 'IN-UT', 'haridwar-dehradun-garhwal', 'Haridwar / Dehradun / Garhwal', 'North India', 30.0, 78.2, 300, 10.0, 'Moderate', '{"name": "Dehradun (Jolly Grant) Airport", "distance_km": 25}'::jsonb, '{"name": "Haridwar Junction / Rishikesh", "distance_km": 0}'::jsonb, 'Dehradun', 45.0, 'Starting point for Char Dham and multiple Himalayan yatras; extensive bus and taxi networks operate in season.[web:273][web:274][web:277]', '{"Spiritual","Pilgrimage_hub","Family"}', '{"Gateway status for Char Dham Yatra (Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath, Badrinath)","Haridwar and Rishikesh ghats and ashrams","Organised yatra packages originating here"}', '{"Short local darshans and Ganga Aarti","Start/end‑point rituals for longer yatras","Booking and orientation for hill pilgrimages"}', 'Serves as basecamp for some of India’s most significant Himalayan pilgrimages while also offering stand‑alone spiritual stays.[web:273][web:274][web:277]', 'Small family‑run dharamshalas favoured by repeat pilgrims | Off‑season quiet days on selected ghats', 'Char Dham window (roughly April/May–Oct, excluding heavy‑rain weeks) plus separate Sep–Apr spiritual‑stay season.[web:273][web:277]', 'Peak monsoon for landslides in upper Garhwal; very hot May days for those not proceeding uphill.', 'Char Dham peak months and major festivals like Kumbh years; spiritual travel trends cite strong demand.[web:273][web:277]', 'Non‑yatra monsoon stretch and some winter weeks, when hill shrines are closed', '{"winter": "8-24\u00b0C (plains level)", "summer": "24-38\u00b0C", "monsoon": "22-30\u00b0C"}'::jsonb, 'Monsoon impacts onward routes more than base towns; still sees heavy showers.[web:274]', '{"Pilgrim_families","Organised_tour_groups","First_time_Himalayan_pilgrims"}', '{"Pilgrim_families": "Char Dham packages commonly bundle Haridwar\u2013Rishikesh orientation nights.[web:273]", "First_time_Himalayan_pilgrims": "Infrastructure, guides and tour operators concentrated here for spiritual tourism.[web:277]"}'::jsonb, 'Char Dham routes demand fitness and altitude tolerance; check health and travel insurance; follow official advisories closely.[web:273][web:277]', 1.0, 2.0, 4, '1–2 nights to acclimatise, attend Aarti and finalise logistics before moving to Char Dham or other Himalayan routes.[web:273]', 'Dharamshalas and ashrams | Budget–mid hotels | Upscale riverfront retreats', 'Vegetarian restaurants and langar/annadan setups for pilgrims.', 8.0, 'City segments busy; main risks relate to onward hill travel and crowds, not crime.[web:277]', 'Good 4G; vital for coordination of hill logistics and weather checks.', 'Jio | Airtel | Vi', 'Ample ATMs and banking services.', 'Hindi | Garhwali | English widely in tourism.[web:273]', FALSE, 'Not required', 'Highly devotional Ganga towns with strong yatra support ecosystem.', 'Kumbh (periodically), Kanwar Yatra and multiple fairs create intense surges.[web:277]', 'Queue discipline and modest dress are expected; respect lane closures and police directions in festival time.', 'Yatra essentials, woollens and spiritual items | Ayurvedic medicines and books', 'Simple bhojanalay thalis | Street chaat and sweets before/after yatra', '{"accommodation_range": [600, 1600], "food_range": [150, 350], "activities_range": [100, 300], "local_transport_range": [200, 500], "total_daily_range": [1050, 2750]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [1600, 3500], "food_range": [250, 600], "activities_range": [150, 400], "local_transport_range": [300, 600], "total_daily_range": [2300, 5100]}'::jsonb, '{"accommodation_range": [3500, 15000], "food_range": [500, 1200], "activities_range": [300, 800], "local_transport_range": [400, 800], "total_daily_range": [4700, 17800]}'::jsonb, 'Experience Haridwar–Rishikesh–Char Dham Spiritual Trail (Meta‑Circuit Node) in Uttarakhand.', 'Seen as the natural jumping‑off point for major Himalayan pilgrimages; spiritual‑tour trend pieces cite strong demand from all age groups.[web:273][web:277]', 'Mentioned in reports on growth of religious tourism and expanded infrastructure under national schemes.[web:272][web:277]', 'Travel in smaller groups where possible, avoid litter during yatras and adhere to hill‑route carrying‑capacity advisories.') ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
